\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 1r\endash 15v \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Poggio Bracciolini:\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Dialogus in avaritiam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dialogus in avariciam Pogij Florentini ad Franciscum Barbarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Antonio Ricio viro prestantissimo Stephanus Novarie S. P. D. dyalogum hunc in avariciam Poggio Florentino nuper editum per me autem Rome scriptum tibi dono do atque largior ut si quando mentem tuam invaserit ardor avaricie qui est communis omnium prelatorum morbus videas \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 Preface: [\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Q\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 uoniam plures mortalium, mi Francisce, non vivunt, sed agunt vitam \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 (f. 1v) Text: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Cum diebus estivis Antonius Luscus, Cracius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [elsewhere corrected by a later hand to \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Cincius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Romanus alijque nonnulli ex Pontificis secretarijs cenarent cum Bartholomeo Politiano \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Sed, cum satis iam collocuti sumus et nox supervenerit, abeundum censeo. Ita omnes consurrexerunt.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Finis.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  Colophon: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit feliciter dialogus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [crossed out: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 novissimus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 in avariciam Pogij Florentini, quem nemo usquam hominum immo nec Franciscus ipse Barbarus vidit. Si quid autem erroris in eo compertum fuerit, non autori sed scriptori ascribat.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  [K. S.: Ed.: Poggio Bracciolini, Dialogus contra avaritiam (de avaritia), ed., Giuseppe Germano, Livorno 1994, pp. 67\endash 93. Bloomfield/Guyot no. 1083 with suppl.] The text is the revised version made by Poggio following the suggestions of Niccol\u242 \'f2 Niccoli. The original version was printed in Basel (1538) and Strasbourg (1513), whereas the revised edition was never printed, although it exists in many manuscripts. See H. Harth, Niccol\u242 \'f2 Niccoli als literarischer Zensor. Untersuchungen zur Textgeschichte von Poggios \u8222 \'84De avaritia\ldblquote , in: Rinascimento n.s. 7 (1978), pp. 29\endash 53 (Marston MS 53 cited as unseen on p. 40), with some readings from the two versions compared on pp. 47\endash 49. The text has been glossed by a contemporary hand, in both Latin and German. \endash  ff. 16r\endash 20v blank.}

