\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Parts I\endash IV all written in Southern Austria, probably ca. 1441 given the contents of ff. 12v\endash 13v. The list of saints on ff. 3r\endash 9r suggests Benedictine interests and a possible connection to Salzburg. Part IV signed by the scribe Georgius Diechercz [?] of Jauntal in Carinthia (colophon on f. 268r). The various parts were bound together at the end of the 15th or beginning of the 16th century. Ownership inscription, s. xv, on f. 269v: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Fr. Oswaldus sant\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [?] ***. Purchased from H. Rosenthal in 1946 by H. P. Kraus who sold it in 1957 to Thomas E. Marston (bookplate).
