\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 f. 2r \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Quingentos decies et bis centum annos\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [sic for \ldblquote minus\rdblquote ] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 uno \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 /\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Annos dic ab adam donec verbum dei caro factum est \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [verses on the span of time between Adam and Christ; Walther, Initia 16015a]; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Notandum decies decem faciunt centum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Decem turbe angelorum lapse sunt de celo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [list of 14 collective nouns, each multiplied by 10 to arrive at number of fallen angels]; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Post inuoca post penthen post cruces postque lucie / Seruant ieiuna sequens feria quarta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (verses on the Wednesday fast for the Ember days of spring [\ldblquote Inuocabit,\rdblquote  the incipit of the introit for the mass of the first Sunday in Lent], summer [Pentecost], fall [Invention of the Holy Cross, 14 September], and winter [feast of St. Lucia, 13 December]). \endash  f. 2v blank.}

