\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 14r\endash 138v \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Jacobus de Voragine: Legenda aurea.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  Prologue:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Uniuersum tempus presentis vite in quattuor distigwuntur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [?] ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Quedam sub tempore peregrinatorum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  Text: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Aduentus domini per quatuor septimas agitur ad significandum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... [concludes in chapter on John the Baptist:] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Magna enim mirabilia mel siluestre et locustas edere pilos cameli induere et huius modi et cetera.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  Ed.: T. Graesse, ed., Jacobi a Voragine Legenda aurea, Leipzig 1846. The legends in the manuscript occur in the following order (with numbers corresponding to Roman numerals in Graesse); many sections lack rubrics. 1, 6 (f. 22r, beginning \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Natiuitas domini nostri ihesu christi secundum carnem ut quid fuit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ...), 13\endash 14, 31\endash 35, 53\endash 54, 70, 72\endash 73, 37, 51, 99, 131, 145, 162\endash 163, 182, 86.}

