\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 139r\endash 171r \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Anonymous letter to John Huss\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 written after the Council of Constance. >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit Tractatus sew epistola missa a quodam doctori Iohanni huss eum corripiendo ut desisteret.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Eloquenti viro domino Iohanni verbi dei seminatori in praga. hec epistola detur fratri suo in christo dilecto pro saluacione in christo ihesu domino nostro. dileccione fraterna in caritate non ficta ante omnia preporrecta ... et desiderans salutem anime mee et anime tue et omnium animarum christianorum. Amen.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  Colophon: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit epistola pulcra missa magistro Iohanni huss finite anno 1439#o\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 11#o\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  crossed out?] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 feria secunda post ascensionem Et 18 die mensis maij.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \endash  Ed.: H. von der Hardt, ed., Rerum Concilii Oecumenici Constantiensis v. 3 (Frankfurt and Leipzig, 1698) pp. 338\endash 391.}

