\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Constitution for the \ldblquote \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 dinghof\rdblquote \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  or \ldblquote \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 colonge\rdblquote \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  of Ingersheim in Alsace\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . First article: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ein vogt ze Blixberg sol ouch alle i\u226 \'e2r ze dinge sin ze Ongersheim an deme nehisten mantage nach sancte Martins tage \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85; second article: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 er sol ouch hie sin alle i\u226 \'e2r an deme mantage, n\u226 \'e2ch der liehtemes, vnd an deme abende \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85; last article: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 der hof sol ouch g\u226 \'e2ben, deme dorfe einen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [K. S.: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 pfarren \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (Alsatian dialect) = bull] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 vnd ein eber.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  A later French translation of this text is edited by Auguste Charles Hanauer, Les constitutions des campagnes de l\rquote Alsace au Moyen-\u194 \'c2ge. Recueil de documents in\u233 \'e9dits, Paris \endash  Strasbourg 1864, pp. 349\endash 354. It is possible that some text has been lost at the beginning.}

