\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 3r1, 33) \plain \f1\caps\lang1033\fs26 2.2 \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Anonymous:\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  Liber duodecim aquarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit liber .12. aquarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 forcium.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Libelli huiusmodi aquarum series\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 .12. splendet capitulis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 Ends f. 4r1, 26: \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 commisceas durescit. si vero duhennec mollescit.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  TK col. 817; DWS no. 1063, etc. The twelve waters in this collection are those printed by Ruska, Osiris VII, pp. 68\endash 72, but in the order 1\endash 8, 10, 9, 11, plus those printed by Berthelot, Chimie, nos. 26, 27 (i.e., two recipes for the last water, Lac virgineum, are supplied).}

