\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 15v2, 35) \plain \f1\caps\lang1033\fs26 2.9: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Argenteus:\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  Geber, or Aristotle, Liber XXX verborum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Liber\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 qui dicitur de .30. verbis.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Iam scis tu qui hanc queris doctrinam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (f. 17v2, 15) \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quod facias donec tuus compleatur numerus. et\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 hoc est verbum .xxx. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash  TK col. 650, 651; DWS no. 84. The work exists in numerous versions and with numerous attributions of authorship.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 17v2, 17) \plain \f1\caps\lang1033\fs26 2.10: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Geber:\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  Liber deitatis sive divinitatis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Liber divinitatis qui est unus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 de .lxx\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Laudes deo sint habenti gratiam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et bonitatem et pietatem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (f. 36v2, 27) \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 In sublimacione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 vero sunt multa signa et in solutione similiter\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 multa et in congelacione similiter multa\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 signa.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  TK col. 813; DWS no. 74, etc. As the rubric in this and other manuscripts indicates, the text is usually found as the first book of the Liber septuaginta of Geber, translated by Gerardus de Cremona, although versions of it differ considerably. The text as it occurs in Paris, BN, MS lat. 7156 was published by Berthelot, Arch\u233 \'e9ologie, 1906, pp. 310\endash 363. However, DWS treats its sections most systematically, her nos. 74\endash 102D. Following her enumeration, the following are present in this codex in the order listed: DWS no. 75 (f. 18r2); DWS no. 102b (f. 19r1); DWS no. 76 (f. 20r1); DWS no. 101 (f. 21r1); DWS no. 85 (f. 21v2); DWS no. 86 (f. 22r2); DWS no. 87 (f. 23r1); DWS no. 88 (f. 23v2); DWS no. 89 (f. 24r2); DWS no. 90 (f. 24v2); DWS no. 91 (f. 25v1); DWS no. 92 (f. 26r1); DWS no. 93 (f. 26r2); DWS no. 94 (f. 27r1); DWS no. 95 (f. 27v2); DWS no. 96 (f. 28r2); DWS no. 97 (f. 29r1); DWS no. 98 (f. 29v1); DWS no. 99 (f. 30r2); DWS no. 100 (f. 30v2); DWS no. 100B with epilogue (f. 31r2); DWS no. 100A (f. 32r1); DWS no. 83 (f. 32v1); DWS no. 78 (f. 33r2); DWS no. 101A, both parts (f. 34r1); DWS no. 101B (f. 34v2); DWS no. 102D (f. 35r2, 16); DWS no. 101C (f. 35r2); DWS no. 101D\endash 102 (f. 36r1), begins as DWS no. 101D, but does not have the ending. Ends f. 36v2, 30, in the same way as the Berthelot version, and as Cambridge, Trin. Coll. MS 1400 (I), f. 22v, as noted in DWS. \endash  f. 36v2, 31\endash 50 blank.}

