\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 67v1, 9) \plain \f1\caps\lang1033\fs26 2.15: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Roger Bacon (?):\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  Alchemy\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Audiant secreti que loquor et dilecti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 verba oris mei. Spiritus ubi vult\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 spirat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (f. 68r1, 18) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et recordati sunt sufficere ad omnes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 egritudines.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Recipe herbam quam tu notasti cum suo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sanguine\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (f. 68r1, 49) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et sic fit lapis cum terra sua de quo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 poteris uti in omnibus vulneribus modo apto.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  TK col. 163, including citation of this codex from L\rquote Art Ancien Catalogue 15; DWS nos. 199, 199ii. The text is partly repetitious and perhaps garbled toward the end, and both endings cited by DWS are supplied. Little 54. A version was printed in: Sanioris medicinae (1603), pp. 285\endash 291.}

