\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 68r2, 1) \plain \f1\caps\lang1033\fs26 2.16(1): \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Anonymous:\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  Collection of eight procedures involving thutia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De separatione thutie.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Accipe de\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 thutia quantum vis et igni eam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  Collection of eight procedures involving thutia, of which the first is printed in: Ze III (1613), 74. The others begin as follows: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Thutia etiam sic preparatur. facias frusta in modum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Accipe thutie eris usti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 utsi \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ?] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 markasite\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Accipe cinerem thutie pulverizatam tere eam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Accipe cinerem eius et imbue illam calcande et viride eris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Accipe cinerem eius et imbue illam calcande de imbibitis istis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Accipe thutiam et tere eam cum oleo et vitro\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Accipe ex ea sublimata et tere eam fortiter.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  Ends f. 68v1, 5.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red255\green102\blue0;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 68v1, 6) \plain \f1\caps\lang1033\fs26 2.16(2): \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Anonymou\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 s:\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  Collection of eight procedures, involving markasita.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De merkasita\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < [sic]. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Markasita est diversi coloris. invenitur similiter argento in albedine\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  Woven into the first of these is a passage printed by J. Ruska as part of: Das Buch der Alaune und Salze. Ein Grundwerk der sp\u228 \'e4tlateinischen Alchemie, hg. v. Julius Ruska, Berlin 1935, section G71, pp. 78\endash 79. The others begin as follows: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Sublimacio almarkasite. Sume eam et tere et acetum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Markasitam bene tritam misce cum nitro\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [?] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et sapone et melle\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Item de marakasita. quam ut prius pluries fuderis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [?]; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Accipe marcasitam albam conbustam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Quomodo tingitur marcasita in colore auri\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Separacio magnesie et marcasite. Accipe de quocumque earum volueris partem unam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (compare TK col. 17); \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Accipe cinerem marcasite aure\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Ends f. 68v2, 48. There are extensive marginalia in a fifteenth-century cursive on f. 68v. \endash  f. 68v2, 49\endash 50 blank.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red255\green102\blue0;}

