\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 76r2, 40) \plain \f1\caps\lang1033\fs26 2.19: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Rasis:\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  De aluminibus et salibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De ferro.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Racio in ferro. Ferrum est de partibus martis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (f. 76v1, 29) \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 tunc operare cum eo.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  TK col. 1388, etc., two portions only, printed by Ruska as G39\endash 40 of his edition of: Das Buch der Alaune und Salze. Ein Grundwerk der sp\u228 \'e4tlateinischen Alchemie, hg. v. Julius Ruska, Berlin 1935, p. 68.}

