\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 34v[23\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ], 13) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 9.9: Anonymous, Treatise on brandy and its properties\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , in Latin, not identified. After one-line space: \u182 \'b6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Item hoc\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [or \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 habemus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ?] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 de aqua Vite. Aqua ardens appellata aqua vite, et aqua vitis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 Both 35v(24\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) and 36v(25\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) have headlines, \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Virtutes aque vite\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , omitted on the intervening page; there is a new rubric on the last line of the last-mentioned page: \u182 \'b6 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Item alia confectio aquae vite. Virtutes eius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , the first part of this rubric being repeated as a headline on f. 37r(25\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ), whereupon the text continues, line 1: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Potest etiam aliter fieri aqua predicta. Recipe tartarum vini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 The passage ends with qualifications concerning fifteen distillations of brandy, line 23: \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Sed in quintadecima facit spumam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [sic] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quam collectam habet solem perfectum et purissimum. Sol.}

