\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 162v[151\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ]) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 9.25: Hippocrates, Secreta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Headline: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipiunt Signa mortui hominis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (line 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipiunt signa mortis, quando in facie ipsius infirmi fuerit pustula, cui non invenitur tactus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (f. 163r[151\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ], 31) \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 occidit ei a privatione sue egritudinis desiderium dei.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  Hippocrates, Secreta, here titled Signa mortis, TK 1168, a text which occurs with many varying incipits.}

