\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (ff. 163v[152\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ]\endash 168v[157\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ]) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 9.26: Anonymous, An extensive medical manual\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , in Latin. On these pages, originally left blank except for ruling and foliation, the principal sixteenth-century annotator and a much later German hand have written several recipes in Latin and German, leaving ff. 167r(155\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 )\endash 168r(156\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) blank, however; not transcribed. f. 169r(157\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ), 1 written in a more pointed and more cursive hand, similar to but perhaps different from the hand which has written the preceding: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De rebus Naturalibus. Sex Res sunt naturales, quevalde operantur ad sanitatem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 Ends f. 198r(186\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ), 36, with a recipe against the colic. \endash  Not located in the literature consulted.}

