\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 198v[187\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ], 1) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 9.27: Albertus Magnus, Secreta mulierum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dilectissime sibi in christo socio et amico.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  The abbreviated name which follows in this copy has defied transcription. (f. 198v[187\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ], 17) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Sicut scribitur secundo de generatione et corruptione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (f. 212v[201\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ], 35) \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 qui cum patre vivit et regnat per infinita seculorum secula Amen. \u182 \'b6 Explicit liber secretorum necnon dicta\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [?] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Magistri Iohannes Gorliczeniss etcetera.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  TK 432, accompanied by the Commentary by Petrus de Ravenna, TK 1498. However, in this copy the explicit attributes the work (the commentary ?) to a certain Iohannes of Gorlitz, who has not been identified in the literature consulted.}

