\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 212v[201\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ], 38) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 9.28: Arnold of Villanova \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 or\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  Constantinus Africanus, Liber de coitu\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et incipit liber Coytus etcetera\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (i.e., title of text on facing page). (f. 213r[201\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ], 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Rerum omnium creator Deus volens genus alium\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [sic, apparently so written in abbreviated form for \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 animalium\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 firmiter ac stabiliter permanere per coytu ac per generacione illud renovari\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (f. 218v[201\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ], 16) \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 postea adde zinziber, piper, cynamonum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [word not read], \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et ad modum nucis.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  TK 272\endash 273. (f. 218v(207\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ), 17) In the principal sixteenth-century hand, the same which wrote nearly identical matter of f. 7r, vide supra: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Vnguentum doctoris Staber Insignis medici Viennensi achademis ad Vlcera et Vlnera mirifice perfectum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  There follows the same list of ingredients written earlier on f. 7r, q.v.; further recipes by the same or a similar hand occur on f. 219r(207\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ), originally blank but for ruling and foliation, not transcribed. ff. 219v(208\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 )\endash 228v(217\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) ruled and foliated, otherwise blank except for a pen trial on the last page.}

