\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 229r[217\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ], 1) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 9.29: John of Rupescissa, De consideratione quinte essentie\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . In the hand which wrote ff. 1\endash 168(157\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Primus liber de consideratione quinte essentie omnium rerum transmutabilium in nomine domini nostri ihesu christi. Incipit liber de famulatu philosophie ewangelio domini nostri ihesu christi et pauperibus ewangelicis = Dixit Salomon Sapientie capitulo xijo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [sic] \u8230 \'85 (f. 270v[259\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ], 6) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 vel sedat, quam nobilissima quinta essentia, vel in eius absentia: Aqua. ardens. laus deo \u182 \'b6 Et sic est finis.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  TK 458, etc., a well-written and straightforward copy. \endash  f. 270v(259\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ), 6 in an originally blank area of the page after a one-line space is hastily written by a cursive gothic hand c. 1550 a list in German of masses, numbers of candles, and amounts of alms to be sung, burned, and distributed on seven holy days of the year for an unnamed individual, ending line 24: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ytem am samstag fan\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [sic] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 vnser frawn ein liecht\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [sic] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 vnd ein almusen ein d\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [i.e., a penny?]. ff. 271r(259\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 )\endash 276v(265\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) originally blank except for ruling and foliation, these pages have been partly used by the principal sixteenth-century hand and possibly others for various short notes and recipes, not transcribed; the original foliation of the codex halts on the final page, which is the last of quire (24).}

