, (2\endash 10)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , (11)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\endash 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [K. S.: original quire formula: II\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  + 6\~VI\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 76\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  + (VII\endash 1)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 89\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  + V\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 99\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ; quire formula after the manuscripts was rebound incorrectly: 9\~V\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 90\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  + (V\endash 1)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 99\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ]   \u183 \'b7   modern pencil foliation (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 1\endash 99\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ), no signatures, no catchwords   \u183 \'b7   195 x 135 [K. S.: writing area: 190\endash 197 x 126\endash 143] with single bordering lines in plumbate or blind   \u183 \'b7   one column except ff. 83r\endash 96v in 2 columns   \u183 \'b7   26\endash 31 lines, no headlines; [K. S.: ff. 94\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 \endash 96\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 22\endash 27 lines]   \u183 \'b7   neatly written in a gothic cursive hand in brown ink, with moderate standard abbreviation; [K. S.: bastarda with loops (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 \endash 93\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ; 94\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 \endash 96\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ; gothic cursive (97\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 \endash 99\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 )]   \u183 \'b7   [K. S.: three hands (A: 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 \endash 93\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ; B: 94\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 \endash 96\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ; C: 97\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 \endash 99\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 )]   \u183 \'b7   large capitals in red at text divisions, sometimes with slight pen ornament, other capitals stroked red throughout, fancy ascenders on top lines transgressing the upper rules and stroked red, similar descenders occasionally below the bottom bordering line, usually not colored; rare correction in the text by the scribe, usually by overwriting; some additions by old hands in the margins. [K. S.: rubricated; one- to three-line lombard initials, partly simply decorated.]}

