\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 81r, 1) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 15.3: Anonymous: Tables of medical weights\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , in Latin and German, not identified. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dis sint scrupelen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [several signs used to abbreviate the unit of weight, one scruple] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 dis sint\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [signs] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 dragman\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [signs, all used to indicate the dram]. Ends f. 81r, 28: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dis sint die gewiecht in der apoteken\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [pen ornament]. (f. 81v, 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Pondera medecine. Granum ordinarium est 24 grana\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [?] \u8230 \'85 Ends f. 82v, 19: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et est pondus Lxxij granorum ordinariorum seu unciarum z\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [?]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  i2 granorum vij\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [pen ornament]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 .\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [pen ornament]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 .\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  Very possibly related to portions of Nicolaus\rquote  De dosibus.}

