\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 94r) 15.7: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Anonymous: Brandy-making, and the sixteen virtues of brandy\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , in German. Upper margin: In a similar, but coarser and perhaps somewhat later cursive: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Wiltu das lebendig\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 wasser machen.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f. 94r1, 1) The headings transcribed below are underlined in red. >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Wiltu das lebendig wasser machen, so nim einen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 firdling, der edlen salben\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (f. 94v2, 14) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Wiltu machen ein\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 wasser, dz g\u252 \'fct ist fur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 al vergifft\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \u8230 \'85 (f. 95r1, 13) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dis ist ein wasser\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 der jugend vnd ein\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 tranck der tugend\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \u8230 \'85 (f. 95v1, 12) With red underlining: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dis sint die tugende des wassers\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < [ornament]; without underlining: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Die erst tugend,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 was do mit besprengt wrt, das blibt wol\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 smacken\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (f. 96v1, 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Die xvi tugent\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (line 5) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 vnd die krafft,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 die der balsam hatt.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Deo Gracias amen.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < Remainder blank. \endash  This is followed in the manuscript by additional procedures and recipes in German written almost illegibly in various scrawling cursive hands of the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries on ff. 97r, 98r\endash 99v, while f. 97v is blank, ending abruptly due to the absence of at least one additional leaf, now missing.}

