\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Probably original binding of stiff parchment over paper boards, flaps over the fore-edge, probably dating from about 1525, conceivably later, as the manuscript contents do not appear to have been bound at the time of writing in any case; flat spine with modern inscription in brown ink, \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Alchemical\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Recipes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , original blue edges.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 1r\endash 4v Lacking. Foliation begins with f. 5, but f. 4 may be pasted down inside front cover. (ff. 5r\endash 6v) Blank except for foliation. (f. 9r, 1) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ad tingendum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [Lead] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 colore\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [of Gold].< \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Recipe x p x c\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [?] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 calcis vive\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 Ends f. 9v, 9: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 fundum calx nigra quam liquefac et est\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [Gold] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 perfectum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 9v, 10) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ad inaurandum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [Lead] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 vel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [Tin]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 .\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Recipe de altero eorum frustum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (f. 9v, 18) \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et si\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 non sit satis pro una vice iteretur bis vel ter.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 9-bis) An inserted slip of paper, 72 x 100, containing closely written additional brief procedures on recto and verso. On the verso, beginning line 4, are the following entries: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Pe.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [Petrus ?] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 dixit quod ex 5 libris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [of Tin] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 positis in potto iacente\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 (line 6) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dicit Helias quod\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [Lead] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 limatum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 in balneo vel in fimo positum dissolvitur in aquam per se.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Doctor Polonus dixit pone rotulos\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [of Lead] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 in filo ferreo sic ut unus non tangat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 alium\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  These individuals are unidentified, but \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Pe. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 is probably to be read as \ldblquote Petrus\rdblquote  and may be the \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Petrus de Delft\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  cited on f. 49-bis, and \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Helias\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  may be \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Helias de ordine beati Francisci\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  cited on f. 48-bis, while the \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Doctor Polonus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  seemingly does not recur.}

