\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 15r, 10) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 27.4: Anonymous, \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Alchemical recipe\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , ten lines in Latin verse. By original text hand:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Spiritum volantem capite / Et in radium solis trahite \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 (f. 15r, 18) \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Tunc in vase proprio ponite / Ut calcinetur optime. Post ipsam suo. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 TK}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  1526 cites a variant of thirty-two verse lines from Paris, BN, MS 14007, of about the same date as the present codex. f. 15v originally blank, but with reading notes added by R\u246 \'f6sel, not transcribed.}

