\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 16r, 1) \plain \f1\caps\lang1033\fs26 27.5: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Anonymous, Alchemical recipes for various processes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , in Latin.\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  SVmmi Philozophi \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [sic] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hermetis ad impleantur et dixit: suaviter ascendit a terra in celum et a celo in terram nutrix eius est terra \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 (f. 22v, 10) \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 testam et invenies regem optimum et virum. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 The rest with light double-cancel: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Et sic est finis huius operis per me Wolffgangum Organistum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [sic]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  de Uznam \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [i.e., Usedom]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  anno 1536 feria secunda ante Simonis et iude \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [i.e., 26 October]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  etc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < Then a note by R\u246 \'f6sel:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Iste Stultius fuit Tran-Scriptor tantum huius nobilissimj et praestantissimi librj non compilator ac tamen se jactat quasi (ut eius nomen indicat) autorem fuisse eiusdem autoris compositio fuit tempore non multo post diluvium. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash  Anonymous, Alchemical recipes for various processes, here ascribed at least in part to {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Hermes}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , not identified; copied by Wolfgang the Organist of Usedom, the scribe of ff. 1\endash 29, on 26 October 1536.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 23r, 1) 27.6: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Theodoric}}\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 , Practica\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , in Latin. By R\u246 \'f6sel\rquote s hand:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Cum illo corpore aquatico quae dicitur Seibach, extrahitur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 A text of six lines, followed by alchemical symbols listed in three lines, and further notes, then seven lines in cipher, followed by a canceled recipe in Latin and cipher, and another canceled, in Latin, then a final one, in German at f. 23v, 22 (17\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 th\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  century):\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Diese Schpruche der Phylosophen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 (f. 24r, 1) By R\u246 \'f6sel\rquote s hand a canceled headline:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Sequitur practica Theodoricalis. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Then a two-line vertical note at right margin:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Dieses ist aus der practick Theodoricj abbreviert worden \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 Then in Wolfgang\rquote s hand, f. 24r, 2: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Recipe in nomine domini venerabilem mercurium et ponas eum in\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  suum alveolum rotundum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 Ends defectively, f. 29v, 19: \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  ut digeratur usque in finalem complecionem. Et ut elucescat rubicudissimus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [sic]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  lapis sanguineus verus tunc illum iterum. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash  Incomplete at the end, perhaps an abbreviation or unidentified extract from the \ldblquote Alchemy\rdblquote  of Theodoric noted by {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezlit[0].8330/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 TK}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  619. Not otherwise located in the literature consulted.}

