\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 66r) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 27.8: Anonymous, Unidentified medical and alchemical recipes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , in Latin and German, occasionally in cipher. Headline (by another early sixteenth-century German hand):\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  aqua ignea vocatur terminus philosophorum. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Line 1, by R\u246 \'f6sel:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Unum et Item. Cartagon. Lunaria. Lumnatica. Vel Barista. Reperi in quodam vetustissimo manuscripto \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 R\u246 \'f6sel\rquote s notes occupy the full page; then, f. 66v, 1, by the same hand which wrote the headline on the preceding page:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Item cementum nobilius super omnia cementa \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 Further recipes and procedures in Latin have been copied by this hand, ending f. 73v, 27: \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 circa hoc circumspectus etcetera.}

