\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 74r, 1) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 27.9: {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Rupertus}}\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 , {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Certum augmentum}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , in German and Latin. Continuing in the same hand, the first line partly cropped by the binder:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Nobilis viri magistri patris Ruperty certum augmentum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [of Gold].\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Nym feyn \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [Gold] \u8230 \'85 Ends f. 74v, 23: \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  ita et argento congruam ultra modum sit laus deo etcetera. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash  Not otherwise identified in the literature consulted.}

