\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 75r, 1) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 27.10: Anonymous, Alchemical recipes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , in German and Latin, partly in cipher. Continuing in the same hand:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Purgacio Saturni funde plumbum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 The recipes and procedures continue through f. 108r, ending with a passage in cipher, f. 108v blank. A new beginning occurs on f. 109r, from which point there are headings in red to each procedure, more lines to the page, and the paper probably changes, but the hand is either the same or a closely similar one. On f. 109r, 1, a recipe is found beginning: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Praeparatio salis amari sequitur capitulum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Accipe sal amarum quae dicitur amarum amari \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 The text ends f. 132v, 13:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  vel margaritarum est enim sulphur sapientum album quae comburit combustione meliorationis. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Remainder blank; then follow three blank flyleaves and the pastedown on which there are further notes in R\u246 \'f6sel\rquote s hand. \endash  All recipes unidentified except that beginning on f. 109r, cited above, which is recorded by TK 23.}

