{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red153\green0\blue204;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Parchment and paper codex in German and Latin, 16\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 o\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , 105 x 85, ff. 87 of which f. 1\endash 3 and 6\endash 19 are of paper, the remainder of parchment, with modern pencil foliation throughout; ff. 1r\endash 21r originally unnumbered, ff. 21v\endash 81v paginated \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 1\endash 121\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  by the copyist in the inks of the manuscript, ff. 82r, 83r, 84r, and 85r numbered respectively \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 122\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 125\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 126\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , and \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 127\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  in the lower outer margins by an early hand, ff. 86\endash 87 originally unnumbered, f. 87 blank, but ff. 83r\endash 87r repaginated \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 124\endash 132\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  in blue ink by Denis Duveen, f. 87 originally blank, one paper leaf missing at the beginning, the pagination not utilized in the description following. No catchwords, no signatures. Collation: (1)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\endash 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , (2)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 18\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (i.e., a paper quire of 14 inserted into a parchment quire of 4 ff.), (3\endash 17)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , (18)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , (19)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 . Single column averaging 82\endash 92 x 73\endash 87, 14\endash 24 lines to the page without ruling or bordering lines. Written throughout in a small, neat gothic cursive in brown inks, additions in a neat italic hand and a rather irregular and sometimes scrawling cursive gothic, both perhaps about 1625. Parchment of good quality, rather thick and a little soiled from handling; paper with a portion of an armorial shield watermark visible at inner margin of f. 10, not identified.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red153\green0\blue204;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Belonged originally to the compiler, Caspar Hartung vom Hoff of Gastein in the province of Salzburg, Austria, who dated the first leaf 1557; annotated by two unidentified hands perhaps about 1625; Denis Duveen, with his inked number 7, acquired from Thomas Heller (bookseller), New York, 1949; Mellon MS 71, acquired with the Duveen collection. De Ricci-Bond 17 (71).
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 SUMMARY: One of the most appealing manuscripts in the Mellon collection, MS 38 is a personal commonplace book combining skillful drawings of apparatus, alchemical texts in German vernacular with noteworthy literary character \endash  some of them in verse \endash  and numerous practical procedures. Its compiler, a man of considerable education, came from the Salzburg region, where he collected some of his procedures from other worthies of the area who were also alchemical practitioners. Caspar Hartung\rquote s Vade mecum may be compared to Mellon MSS 20, 30, 40, 44, and 92, all of which contain large numbers of practical procedures and many of which are of Germanic origin. Also, its numerous and beautiful drawings may be compared with other extended series such as the rough, but contemporary Italian group found on the flyleaves of Mellon MS 36, the set partly inspired by Biringucci in Mellon MS 51, and the very delicate, but much later drawings in Mellon MS 73. The two longer alchemical poems in the manuscript, \ldblquote Die Reimen der Philosophen\rdblquote  beginning on f. 32r, and \ldblquote Die Reimen Hermetis\rdblquote  beginning on f. 74r, have not been identified and do not recur in the Mellon collection.}

