\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 [K. S.: Herwig Buntz, Die europ\u228 \'e4ische Alchimie vom 13. bis zum 18. Jahrhundert, in: Alchimia. Ideologie und Technologie, ed. Emil Ernst Ploss, Heinz Roosen-Runge, Heinrich Schipperges et al., M\u252 \'fcnchen 1970, p. 119\endash 210, here p. 183, n. 162 (MS mentioned with old number Cod. 17 [71])   \u183 \'b7    Kristeller, Iter Italicum 5, p. 290.]}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red153\green0\blue204;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Nineteenth-century straight-grained black morocco, gilt single-line perimetric border for each cover and spine, gilt dentelles, and border of the same tools at head and foot of spine, modern tan leather spine label, with legend:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  HARTUNG V. HOFF. VADE MECUM. MANUSCRIPT AUSTRIA 1557.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red153\green0\blue204;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Front pastedown: This and the recto of the first front flyleaf are of marbled paper, otherwise blank; on the verso of the first flyleaf are Duveen\rquote s characteristic number and booksellers\rquote  penciled notes in a modern Germanic hand; the second front flyleaf blank.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red153\green0\blue204;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 f. 1r, 1 \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Caspar Hartung vom Hoff: Das Vade mecum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , a commonplace book of alchemical and medicinal materials, consisting of mostly shorter prose and verse sections, often with excellent drawings, thirty-one in all, of alchemical equipment, written in 1557, and with additions written about fifty years later. At left of a pen sketch of an alchemical flask, and partly in cipher: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dieses verendert sich, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... Line 5, after cipher continuing on same line at right of flask\rquote s neck: ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 auf ain sant oder ashen.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 1v, 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Register. Das buechlin Gebri des philosophen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... Ends f. 3r, 5:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  brieff verborgen tragen \endash  ro\u223 \'df muthig machen. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Remainder of f. 3 blank. (f. 4r, 1) Written as a title page:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Das Vade mecum Caspar Harttungs vom hoff au\u223 \'df der Gastein: 1557. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 By a later, early seventeenth-century hand: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Verus Mercurius et cetera sequitur. Ante debitam coctionem \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 5v, 13) ...\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  sed tu et \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [erroneously used]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  hortum et duos vates tertium postulantes probe noscere debes. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 End of seventeenth-century script. (f. 6r, 1) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Geber, Buch der Heiligkeit oder Heimlichkeit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . In the original hand:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Hie facht sich an das buch des k\u252 \'fcnigs Gebri auss Hispania, ain buch der haimlichait \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 8r, 3)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Das I. capitel in das buch Gebri der hailigkait oder haimligkait. Allen vnd ieden, die do in diser hailigen kunst studirn \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 17v, 9)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Das neundt capitel von gemerung der vorgemelten ertzne\u255 \'ff durch seinen aignen samen. Der dritt weg der merung der ertzne\u255 \'ff ist, das mag gemert werden durch seinen aigen samen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 19r, 4) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ... ist ain gmain gut, das niendert kain philosophi also cl\u228 \'e4rlich geseczt habe. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 A final heading occurs on f. 19r, 6:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Volgt das lampen liecht zu machen, dz es brenne ain gancze monat \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... Ends f. 19v, 9: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ... mit coralle, der roten ist auch ain gemein\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  [K. S.: Joachim Telle, Geber, in: Verfasserlexikon, vol. 2, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1980, col. 1105\endash 1109, here col. 1107\endash 1109 (MS mentioned col. 1108).]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 This concludes the paper leaves, which may have been a slightly later insertion into the volume, although written by Hartung. (f. 20r) The page has a fine pen drawing of an oven with this heading:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Inventio moderna furni ad coquendum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  On the following pages are further drawings of apparatus with an extended text describing procedures for making oil of vitriol, ending f. 32r, 9: ...\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  das nindert kain philosophi also clerlich geseczt haben.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 32r, 10)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Die reimen der philosophen. Rath was ist das. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Then, in verse:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain man, ain weib vnd dern kains / Son, vatter, mutter alles ains \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... This begins an extended alchemy in verse illustrated with many fine drawings of apparatus, with headings for a Practica, a Theorica, \ldblquote Malchamech philosophus,\rdblquote  and ending, f. 37r, 1:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Arnoldus. O gebenede\u255 \'ffte gr\u255 \'ffenhait, die du alle ding gebirst. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (line 7) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ... vnd recht, thustu anderst, so n\u252 \'fcczet es nichts. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Illustration on lower half of page, and illustrations of several flasks and other pieces of equipment on f. 37v. (f. 38r, 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Die k\u252 \'fcnigin Arnoldj. Jeczo hastu gelernet das we\u255 \'ff\u223 \'df machen. Nun ist vom roten zu sagen. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... Illustration follows at lower half of page after line 12, while text continues on f. 38v, ending line 19: ...\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Al\u223 \'dfdan bedarff man die selbe weisse nit auss ziehen, sonder kochs, bis gar rot wirt.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 39r, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain g\u246 \'f6ttliche, hailige kunst zumachen pars cum parte, das bestendig ist \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 41v, 11)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  so hastu rain vnd gut gold vff den kauff, wahin du wilt. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 42r, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain vleissige arbait vnd ain nutzliche ainem armen gesellen zumachen. So du das oleum vitrioli, wie vorgemelt, gebrent hast, so nim die schwarcz erd au\u223 \'df dem krug \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 43r, 11)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain compass auff edel gestain. So schaw vmb ain magneten, der flach ist \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... On f. 43v is a schematic drawing of a compass card. (f. 44v, 9)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain schone \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [sic]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  albaz zumachen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 46r, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Oleum antimonij zumachen. La\u223 \'df den antimonium vliessen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 47r, 11) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Salarmoniac auff das best vnd rainest. Nim ru\u223 \'df, der so fleust in caminen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 48r, 5) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tutia machen. Nim calcinirten tartarum, ble\u255 \'ff aschen\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 vnd waideschen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... On f. 48v is a drawing of an oven for calcination; f. 49r, 1:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain gut gradier wasser vff pars cum parte. Nim 1 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [pound]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  rohen vitriol, den calcinier auff die\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 gilb, sto\u223 \'df in klain \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... On f. 50r is a drawing of an oven for distillation; f. 50v, 3:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain wasser, das alle metall vffl\u246 \'f6set. Recipe 4 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [pounds]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  allun, den calcinir vff ainem plech \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 51v, 5)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Mein aqua vite. Nim 1 lot cimat \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 52v, 3) ...\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ist gut f\u252 \'fcrn schlag vnd pestilencz. Ain ander costlich guth aqua vite vom apotecker zu Regenspurg: Nim valerian, tormentill, diptami, wurcz an iii lot cicorea \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 53r, 10)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Diss obgemelt wasser ist zu allen zufelligen kranckhaiten gut. Von Jacob I\u223 \'dfrahel zu Regenspurg. Volget ain ander oleum antimonj. Nim \u189 \'bd \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [pound]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  antimonj, la\u223 \'df vliessen vnd nim \u188 \'bc\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [pound]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  tartari, klain zerstossen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 54r, 11)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Schwebel fix machen. Nim rohen schwebel, der rot ist der best, der v\u223 \'df dem ercz gezogen wirt, mit essich zersto\u223 \'df in klain \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 55v, 10)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Oleum von mastix. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... There is a drawing of distillation apparatus on f. 56r. (f. 56v, 11)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Muscaten \u246 \'f6l. Nogelin Macis Recipe: Nim muscaten, klain zerstossen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 57r, 4)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Gute venedische saiffen. Nim gar frischen vngelesten kalch, 12 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [pounds] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 brich in aschen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (f. 59r, 8)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Schaiden im guss. Nim 8 lot antimonium \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... There is a sketch of a piece of apparatus on f. 58v. (f. 59v, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Schmeltzen von allen farben glas auff glass. So hab acht, erstlich l\u246 \'f6t klaine tr\u228 \'e4tlin kre\u252 \'fccz wei\u223 \'df \u252 \'fcber a.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (in)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  a.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (nder)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 , wie\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 hie steet \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 60r, 13)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Burruss machen. Nim tartarum, den calcinir vff alle wei\u223 \'df \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 61r, 16)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Metridat machen. Nim kran\u246 \'f6glin parisk\u246 \'f6rnlin \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 61v, 15)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Die quintam essentiam auss dem wein zuziehen on fe\u252  \'fcr. So nim ba\u255 \'ffle, schnitte brott, fa\u223 \'df an ain faden oder schnur vnd oben\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 62r)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  darauff fa\u223 \'df ain badschwam vnd wider schnitte brot \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... There is a drawing of a wine barrel on f. 62r. (f. 62v, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Distillierung der edlen wassern von den edlen kre\u252 \'fctern. Mit farb gschmack vnd \u246 \'f6l zubehalten, das man sunst\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 die zeit nit kann behalten \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 63v, 12)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Antimonium vnd schwebel auss dem ertz saigeren. So mach ain tieffe gruben in die erden \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... There is a drawing of apparatus on f. 64r. (f. 64v, 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Das silber zumachen, das durchsichtig wie ain cristall wirt. Nim 3 lot aqua fort vnd 1 lot fin silber, la\u223 \'df im aqua fort solnirn, vnd wan es gar solnirt ist \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (line 14) ...\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  dursichtig wie ain cristall. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 On f. 65r is a drawing of an oven depicting the use of the\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Sigillum Hermetis. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 65v, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain wunderbarlich oleum tartarj zumachen.\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Nim tartarus, calcinir den im reuerber ofen mit vlei\u223 \'df \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... There are small drawings of vessels on f. 65v. (f. 66r, 7)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Kr\u252 \'fceg zum vitriol ol vnd andern starcken wassern brennen. Nempt 1 tail gestossen kisling stain \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 67r, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Den laim anmachen zu den widn\u246 \'f6fen. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (line 7)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Test. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (line 15)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Bain giessen. Nim das bain, was bain du wilt,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 fail dz vff dz klainest \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 68v, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Buchstaben auff dem pergamen ausstilcken. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (line 8)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  M\u246 \'f6ssing vnd kupfer we\u255 \'ffss zusieden. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 69r, 3) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Zu kettinen ziehen. Volgt ain r\u252 \'fcstung, wie man h\u252 \'fcpsch kettin ziehen soll, von m\u252 \'fcllstain brunnen kettin oder ander\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sort \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... At the foot of the page is a drawing of a hand-cranked machine for forming chain-links (?). (f. 69v, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain luna fixa. Conrad de Bibrach. Nim arsenicum crudum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (line 16) ...\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  so wirstu s\u255 \'ff schwer vnd fix finden, die tingier dan, wie du waist.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 70r, 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Vocabularius. Aurum. Sol. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Then six symbols for Gold opening a vocabulary of alchemical terms and symbols which closes on f. 73r, 8, the remainder of the page blank. (f. 73v, 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Speculum. Darumb so ist von n\u246 \'f6ten, dz vnser stain werd ausgezogen\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 aus der natur zwa\u255 \'ffer c\u246 \'f6rper \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... Ends line 8: ...\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  in philosophisch gold vnd in philosopisch \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [sic]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  silber. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Remainder of f. 73v blank. (f. 74r, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Die reimen Hermetis. Ower bring mir ain nackends weib / wan vnselig was mein erster leib \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... The poem, 340 verses in rhyming couplets, ends f. 77v, 3:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  das sagen wir Gott im himmel danck. Finis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [flourish]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 .\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [K. S.: Within the poem f. 76r\endash 77r \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Turba philosophorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (Spr\u252 \'fcche vom alchemistischen Stein). Joachim Telle, \u8218 \'82Turba philosophorum\rquote , in: Verfasserlexikon, vol. 9, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1995, col. 1151\endash 1157, here col. 1155\endash 1156 (MS mentioned col. 1155).] (f. 77v, 4)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Die zwelff zaichen. Die 3 irdische zaichen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [three alchemical symbols]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 . Die 3 w\u228 \'e4sserige zaichen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [three alchemical symbols]. After two further lines devoted to characterizations of three signs each follows a table, headed by the signs of the principal planets and followed by two triple rows of signs, arabic numerals 1\endash 23, and the twenty-three letters of the Latin alphabet \endash  in other words, a simple cipher code system, ending line 16, not transcribed. (f. 78r, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain labor abbatis Sancti Petri kompt vom bischoff von Saltzburg vnd schwert, s\u255 \'ff se\u255 \'ff warhafft vnd gerecht. Erstlich mach ain crocum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [of Iron]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  also. Nim gefeilt eisen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 79r, 1) ...\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  so magstu darmit verg\u252 \'fclden, also hat es herr magister von Chur gefunden gerecht.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 79r, 4)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain cement des bischoffs von Saltzburg. Er sagt, er er \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [erroneously repeated]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  brauche den salarmoniac \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (line 17) ...\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Jedes mal 3 stund. Das ist sein cement.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 79v, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ain cement partis cum parte. Nim gefeilt stachel oder guts eisen, dz kain ander metall\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 darunter ist weder zin noch kupfer \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (f. 80r, 1)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Brieff verborgen tragen. Nim ain\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 blater haut vnd den brieff leg vnden an die solen des blo\u223 \'dfen fu\u223 \'df vnd spann die blater\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 haut dar\u252 \'fcber \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (line 7)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ross muthig machen. Wan die ro\u223 \'df melancolisch vnd m\u252 \'fced\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sind oder alters halb nimmer geen oder taugen wollen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (line 19) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 darvon wirt dz pferd\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 muthig, springt vnd laufft hurtig, vnd gillt sein gelt zuverkauffen. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 80v, 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Mercurium recht sublimirn. Nim vitriol \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... The recipe ends line 16, the final entry in the original hand of the MS; it is followed, line 17, by a text in the seventeenth-century italic hand:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Mercurius sese loquitur. Constans ego sum constanti artifici \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... Ends f. 81r, 14, not transcribed; on f. 81v is a heading in another less good italic hand:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Tabula smaragdina Hermetis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , which is followed by a longer passage written in a scrawling late sixteenth-century or seventeenth-century gothic cursive, beginning:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Das gehoertt furhin zuo den philos\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 of\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 )\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 en re\u255 \'ffmen vnd Herme\u223 \'df, der beschre\u255 \'ffbts. Alle ding send beschaffen von ainem ainigen durch den willen vnd gepott aines ainigen, die son ist der vatter, der\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 mon ist die mutter \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... Ends f. 82r, 17:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  zwa\u255 \'ff hundert tussent mal tussent. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 82v, 1) In the fine seventeenth-century italic:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Centrum Mercurij. Centrum meum\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26\cf6  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 est cor omnium fixissimum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... Ends line 15, not transcribed; written in a scrawling cursive, beginning on f. 83r, 1, is:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Fur das blued rinen au\u223 \'df der haimblihhait \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [sic]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 . Recipe. Ain aisene nu\u223 \'df \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... Another recipe on f. 83v, 1, in the same hand, begins:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Ein stich Pflaster vom Kaiser Friderich f\u252 \'fcr stich vnnd wunden. Recipe. Ain vierting \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... On f. 84v, 9, is a recipe against fever, which closes on f. 85r, 2, the last entry in the scrawling hand; then the fine italic hand concludes the manuscript, beginning on line 3:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Amititiae \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [sic]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Mercurij candor. Quicquid mecum est amo, sicut amicum et quicquid mecum nascitur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... On f. 86r, 13, is another heading:\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Hic mater natura prodit suum filium Mercurium. Est mihi unus filius talis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... Ends f. 86v, 13: ...\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  ergo quicunque aliquid inde haberj velit, omnia enim secreta hic prae oculis habet. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 f. 87, blank except for numbers in late hands is somewhat wormed. \endash  [K. S.: Bernhard Haage, Das \u8222 \'84Kunstb\u252 \'fcchlein\ldblquote  des Alchemisten Caspar Hartung vom Hoff. In Abbildung und Transkription (Litterae. G\u246 \'f6ppinger Beitr\u228 \'e4ge zur Textgeschichte 39), G\u246 \'f6ppingen 1975.]}

