{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 f. 3r \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Andreas Oberlender: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Probie\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 rb\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 \u252 \'fc\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 chlein, 1532\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Written as a title in a bold and practiced gothic script: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ein Kunstlich vndt Gerecht Probier B\u252 \'fcchlein vff Allerle\u255 \'ff Ertz vndt Metall. Durch \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [flourishes] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Andreas Oberlender 1532.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ff. 3v\endash 4v blank except for red bordering lines. (f. 5[1]r, 1) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Wie man Capellenaschen machen soll. Nimb aschen, der durch zuvor Laugen gemacht, thue die in ein fa\u223 \'df, geu\u223 \'df wa\u223 \'dfer daran, rhure es wohl vmb \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 With this process begins a group of almost two hundred fifty alchemical procedures relating to metallurgy and mining processes. The group ends on f. 121(117)v with a procedure headed: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Da\u223 \'df Ble\u255 \'ff au\u223 \'df den Teste zubringen, Thomas Gregorius. Nimb rein vngeleschten Kalck, weidaschen vnnd todnkopff, zusto\u223 \'df den toden kopff vnd die weidaschen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 On f. 122(118)r is a table of alchemical terms and their symbols, followed on the next pages through f. 131r by an alphabetical index of contents to the preceding; ff. 131v\endash 132v are blank. On f. 133(129)r occurs a new title: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tractat von Saltzwergenn. Wie man alle Saltzsehlen oder Saltzwa\u223 \'dfer durch vnterschiedene Arth Probieren und ieden halt der Salzbrunnen erforschenn soll\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 This brief tract ends on f. 142v, not transcribed; there are small drawings in red of vessels on ff. 136r and 137r. f. 143r is blank except for bordering lines; a later hand has added a supplement beginning on f. 144(140)r: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hans Knabens Figirung der solarischen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [Sulphur] \u8230 \'85 Ends f. 144(140)v, 3: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dieser Hans Knabe gewohnt an der Schlesischen grentze im M\u228 \'e4hrischen geb\u252 \'fcrge in einem St\u228 \'e4ttlein mit Nahmen L\u228 \'e4merstatt nicht weit von Troppau.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  Remainder blank. A brief \ldblquote Bergarbeit\rdblquote  has been copied in the same hand, followed by four brief recipes, on ff. 145r\endash 146r, not transcribed. ff. 146v\endash 147v are blank except for bordering lines; two recipes are written in the same hand on f. 148r\endash 148v, not transcribed. Final pastedown, of more recent paper and a modern insertion, is blank. \endash  Andreas Oberlender: Probierb\u252 \'fcchlein, 1532, an unsigned later copy executed about 1600, with a few additions, not otherwise identified.}

