\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Paper (watermarks similar to Briquet Lettre P 8619 [K. S.: 1477/78] and 8625 [K. S.: 1484/90]), ff. iii (paper) + 401 + iv (paper), 276 x 208 (222 x 145) mm. Written in two columns  of 39\endash 42 lines; frame-ruled in ink or lead, with some double inner vertical guide-lines and an occasional additional ruling in lower margin   \u183 \'b7   I\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , II\endash XL\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (+ 3 leaves at end; structure uncertain). Remains of catchwords along lower edge of folio in gutter; most trimmed   \u183 \'b7   Written in a well formed running hand [K. S.: Bastarda] by a single scribe who has been identified [K. S.: by Selmer] as Freiherr von Greifenclav (see Provenance). Divisions for indexing carefully noted in margins   \u183 \'b7   Large penwork initials of mediocre quality, in red and blue; foliage designs in center of letters and penwork borders, in red, are sometimes accompanied by vulgar green dots. Many simple initials, 7- to 1-line, in red or blue; running titles in red. Rubricated throughout.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 [K. S.: restored and newly bound   \u183 \'b7   25 watermarks: letter P: watermark twins (P1 and P2 with variation of watermark twins P6 and P7): Buchstabe P (P1): =\~WZIS DE1185-S372_14 (1470/1480, o.\~O.) and Buchstabe P (P2): =\~WZIS DE1185-S372_13 (1470/1480), ~\~WZIS DE8100-PO-108472 (1476/1477, K\u246 \'f6ln), ~\~WZIS DE2730-PO-108477 (1477, Rottweil), ~\~WZIS DE2730-PO-108473 (1480, Mainz), ~\~WZIS DE4500-Wx_218_13 (s. XV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 4/4\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ); watermark twins (P3 and P4): Buchstabe P (P3): very similar WZIS DE4500-PO-108336 (1477, K\u246 \'f6ln), ~\~WZIS DE4500-PO-108396 (1478, Zabern) and Buchstabe P (P4): ~\~WZIS DE6405-PO-108412 (1479, Baden-Baden), ~\~WZIS DE6300-PO-108398 (1480, Frankfurt am Main); watermark twins (P5 and P15): Buchstabe P (P5): =\~WZIS DE4500-PO-107536 (1482, Ehrenbreitstein), =\~WZIS NL8370-PO-107551 (1479, Utrecht), =\~WZIS DE2040-PO-107981 (1481, Kleve), very similar WZIS DE8100-PO-107541 (1481, L\u246 \'f6wen), very similar WZIS DE8100-PO-107537 (1481, L\u246 \'f6wen) and Buchstabe P (P15): =\~WZIS DE8730-PO-107540 (1480, Wesel), very similar WZIS AT3800-PO-107563 (1478, Selz, Stift), very similar WZIS NL8370-PO-107558 (1479, Utrecht), very similar WZIS DE1785-PO-107556 (1479, Kleve), very similar WZIS DE8100-PO-107567 (1481, L\u246 \'f6wen); watermark twins (P8 and P9): unidentifiable, Buchstabe P (P9): ~\~WZIS DE2040-PO-113613 (1478, D\u252 \'fcren), ~\~WZIS NL8370-PO-114075 (1478, Utrecht), ~\~WZIS DE4500-PO-113607 (1487, K\u246 \'f6ln) (details differing); watermark twins (P10 and P11): unidentifiable, Buchstabe P (P10): type WZIS DE4500-PO-113490 (1487, Vullessheym), type WZIS DE8100-PO-113497 (1488, K\u246 \'f6ln); watermark twins (P13 and P14): Buchstabe P (P13): very similar WZIS DE9090-PO-112331 (1477, Xanten) and Buchstabe P (P14): =\~WZIS NL0360-PO-111578 (1478, Culemborg), =\~WZIS DE2040-PO-111581 (1480, Lulsdorf), =\~WZIS DE4500-PO-111580 (1481, K\u246 \'f6ln), =\~WZIS DE4500-PO-111579 (1482, D\u252 \'fcsseldorf), =\~WZIS DE2040-PO-112330 (1487, D\u252 \'fcsseldorf); watermark twins (P16 and P18 with variant P19): Buchstabe P (P16): =\~WZIS BE3075-PO-112716 (1479, Gent), =\~WZIS DE9090-PO-111892 (1482, Xanten), =\~WZIS DE9090-PO-111889 (1482, Xanten) and Buchstabe P (P18 with variant P19): =\~WZIS DE3285-PO-111884 (1480, Marburg), =\~WZIS DE2730-PO-111883 (1481, Marburg), very similar WZIS BE3075-PO-112715 (1479, Gent); watermark twins (P17 and P 22): Buchstabe P (P17): =\~WZIS FR8040-PO-112976 (1480, Hugeshofen, Kloster), =\~WZIS DE4500-PO-111911 (1483, D\u252 \'fcsseldorf), =\~WZIS DE2040-PO-111920 (1484, Stein am Rhein) and Buchstabe P (P22): =\~WZIS BE3075-PO-112713 (1480, Gent), =\~WZIS NL8370-PO-112995 (1481, Utrecht), =\~WZIS DE2040-PO-111921 (1484, o. O.); watermark twins (P20 and P21): Buchstabe P (P20): =\~WZIS DE9090-PO-110580 (1479, Xanten), =\~WZIS DE9090-PO-111214 (1480, Xanten), =\~WZIS NL8370-PO-111399 (1480, Middelburg, Seeland), =\~WZIS DE0960-4Inc641.12_l4 (16.08.1482, K\u246 \'f6ln, Drucker: Ulrich Zell) and Buchstabe P (P21): =\~WZIS DE9090-PO-111210 (1479, Xanten), =\~WZIS DE9090-PO-111212 (1480, Xanten), =\~WZIS NL8370-PO-111400 (1480, Middelburg, Seeland), =\~WZIS DE2040-PO-110551 (1480, Kleve), =\~WZIS NL8370-PO-111310 (1481, Utrecht); watermark twins (P23 and P24): Buchstabe P (P23): =\~WZIS DE2040-PO-111201 (1481, Hambach), =\~WZIS BE3075-PO-111321 (1481, Gent), =\~WZIS DE2040-PO-111200 (1482, Kleve) and Buchstabe P (P24): =\~WZIS DE2040-PO-110550 (1482, Kleve); Buchstabe P (P25): very similar (details differing) WZIS DE2730-PO-26721 (1483, o.\~O.)   \u183 \'b7   quire formula: (III+3)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  + (IV+1)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 18\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  + 37 V\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 388\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  + (V+3)\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 401\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22    \u183 \'b7   loss of text at the beginning of the first and at the end of the last quire   \u183 \'b7   modern foliation in lead (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 1\endash 401\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 )   \u183 \'b7   writing area: 21,1\endash 22,5 x 14,2\endash 15   \u183 \'b7   two columns   \u183 \'b7   35\endash 44 lines   \u183 \'b7   bastarda with loops   \u183 \'b7   one hand (including marginal notes and additions)   \u183 \'b7   rubricated; 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 13-line pen-flourished initial in red, blue, green and brown, 4\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 8-line pen-flourished initial in red, blue, green and brown, 56\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 14-line pen-flourished initial in red, blue and green, 95\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 12-line pen-flourished initial in red, blue, green and brown, 130\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 12-line pen-flourished initial in red, blue, green and brown, 212\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 9-line pen-flourished initial in red, blue and black, 215\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 6-line initial in red and blue, 238\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 11-line pen-flourished initial in red, blue and black, 255\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 13-line initial in red and blue, 304\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 11-line pen-flourished initial in red, blue and black, 315\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 12-line initial in red and blue, 377\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 13-line initial in red and blue, 237\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 : 4-line red-black lombard initial, one- to four-line lombard initials in red and blue; running titles in red in the heading; marginal \lquote nota\rquote  sign (pointing hand); manuscript shows 