\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 1ra\endash 237va \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Birgitta Suecica:\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  Revelationes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Liber 1\endash 5. (f. 1ra\endash 54va) Liber 1. (f.\~1ra\endash rb) Table of Contents cap. LIII\endash LX: \u9553 \'a6\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 mirabilia continentur.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Capittulum liii.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Verba angeli ad sponsam de spiritu cogitacionum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 predicanda per dei amicos personis ignorantibus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Capittulum lx. Expliciunt rubrice primi libri celestis revelacionum dei\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 beate Birgitte divinitus revelate.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < [K. S.: (f. 1rb\endash 3vb) [\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Matthias Lincopiensis]: Prolog\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .] >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Sequitur prologus in libris celestibus revelacionum dei Beate Birgitte divinitus revelatus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Stupor et mirabilia audita sunt in terra nostra. Mirabile si quidem erat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 [K. S.: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 qui tempore et loco una voce cordis sui monicionem in melius experti, nisi ingrati fuerint Christo, ab ipso factam ad verba eis ab ipso missa fatebantur.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 4ra) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit liber primus celestis revelacionum dei beate Birgitte, principisse de regno Suecie, divinitus revelatis. Verba domini nostri Ihesu Christi ad suam electam sponsam dilectissimam de certificacione sue excellentissime incarnacionis et improbacione prophanacionis et fractionis fidei nostre et baptismi et qualiter ad sui dilectionem invitat prefatam dilectam sponsam. Primum capitulum. Liber primus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ego sum creator celi et terre et unus in deitate cum patre et sancto spiritu, ego, qui prophetis et patriarchis loquebar et quem ipsi expectabant\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 usquequo veniant ad locum, qui michi placuerit.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit liber primus celestis revelacionum dei beate Birgitte, principisse Nerecie de regno Suecie, divinitus revelatus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f. 54va\endash 93vb) Liber 2. (f. 54va\endash 56ra) Table of Contents cap. I\endash XXX. (f.\~56ra) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit liber celestis revelacionum dei secundus. Informacio filii ad sponsam contra dyabolum et responsio filii ad sponsam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et qualiter bapizatis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  morientibus infra annum discrecionis datur regnum celorum. Capitulum I.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f. 56rb) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Filius loquebatur ad sponsam dicens: Quando dyabolus temptat te, dic ei ista tria: Verba dei non possunt esse nisi vera\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sed cum tempus fuerit loquendi.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit liber secundus revelacionum celestium dei beate Beate \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  Birgitte divinitus revelatus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f. 93vb\endash 124vb) Liber 3. (f. 93vb\endash 95va) Table of Contents cap. I\endash XXXIV. (f. 95va) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit liber tercius celestis revelacionum dei beate Birgitte, principisse Nerecie de regno Suecie, divinitus revelatus. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 95vb) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Monicio et informacio de modo tenendo in victu et vestitu et oracione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et qualiter in omnibus exerceat officium episcopale. Capitulum I.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f. 95vb) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ihesus Cristus, deus et homo, qui venit in terram assumere humanitatem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 corpus vero non interfici sed mundari per abstinenciam, ut verba dei per illud diffundantur.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit liber celestis tercius revelacionum dei beate Birgitte divinitus revelatus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f. 124vb\endash 212ra) Liber 4. (f. 124vb\endash 130va) Table of Contents cap. I\endash CXXX. (f. 130va) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit liber quartus celestis revelacionum dei beate Birgitte divinitus revelatus. Verba Iohannis ewangeliste ad sponsam, qualiter nullum opus est sine remuneracione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et qualiter debeat contempnere divicias et honores propter deum. Capitulum primum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f. 130vb) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Apparuit sponse persona quedam, cuius crines videbantur circumcisi cum opprobrio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et sepelietur et iudicabitur cum leprosis et non sedebit cum iudicantibus orbem.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit liber quartus celestis revelacionum beate Birgitte divinitus revelatus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f. 212ra\endash 237va) Liber 5. (f. 212ra\endash 215ra) Table of Contents Interrogatio I \endash  Revelatio XIII. (f. 215ra) Prologue: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit prologus quinti libri questionum celestium revelacionum qui dicitur liber questionum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit quintus liber celestium revelacionum Christi ad beatam Birgittam de regno Suecie\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 prout alios libros revelacionum translatare solitus erat. Et sic est finis prologi.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 215va) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit liber quintus celestium revelacionum, qui intitulatur liber questionum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Vidi thronum in celo, in quo sedebat dominus Ihesus Christus ut iudex. Ante cuius pedes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [sedebat] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 stabat virgo Maria et in circuitu throni erat exercitus angelorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quam dulcis et suavis sum ego deus. Itaque, cum veneris ad ista loca, ostendam tibi plura.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit liber quintus questionum revelacionum a Christo sponse sue beate Birgitte, principisse Nerecie de regno Suecie. Deo laus et gloria in secula seculorum. Amen.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <] \endash \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26\cf17  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Beinecke MS 24 appears in the critical edition (MS H). Undhagen believes that the Yale codex was copied from MS O\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 a\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (Katrineholm, Ericsbergs slottsbibliotek (Library of Ericsberg Castle). For a detailed analysis see Undhagen, p. 179, n. 7. and p. 199. \endash  [K. S.: Ed.: Book 1: Carl-Gustaf Undhagen (ed.), Sancta Birgitta. Revelaciones. Book I with Magister Mathias\rquote  prologue, Uppsala 1978 (MS mentioned p. IX; brief description of MS and text p. 178 f.); Book 2: Carl-Gustaf Undhagen / Birger Bergh (ed.), Sancta Birgitta. Revelaciones. Book II, Stockholm 2001; Book 3: Ann-Mari J\u246 \'f6nsson (ed.), Sancta Birgitta. Revelaciones. Book III, Stockholm 1998; Book 4: Hans Aili (ed.), Sancta Birgitta. Revelaciones. Book IV, Stockholm 1992; Book 5: Birger Bergh (ed.), Sancta Birgitta. Revelaciones. Book V, Uppsala 1971. Ulrich Montag, Birgitta von Schweden, in: Verfasserlexikon, vol. 1, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1978, col. 867\endash 869, here col. 868 f., and vol. 11, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 2004, col. 258. CALMA vol. 2,4, p.\~410 f., no. 1.]}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [K. S.: ff. 237vb\endash 304va \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Birgitta Suecica: Revelationes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Liber 8 (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Liber caelestis imperatoris ad reges\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ). (f. 237vb\endash 252rb) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Alfonsus Giennensis: Epistula Solitarii ad reges\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (f. 237vb\endash 238ra) Table of Contents cap. I\endash VII. (f.\~238ra) On a glued-in note: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Questio. Reprehenduntur illi qui ex abrupto improvise nullo examine precedente approbant aut reprobant personas se asserentes se\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [!]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  habere visiones et revelaciones divinas. Capitulum primum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [Text continues in the lower margin:] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit epistola solitarii ad reges vel examinacio visionum tam theorice quam practice. Registrum super examinacione visionum tam theorice quam practice quere circa finem libri.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f.\~238ra) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Serenissimi reges et utinam veri reges in Christo, domini mei precarissimi, supplici et humilima reconmendacione premissa\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quia cum exarserit in brevi ira eius, beati omnes, qui puro corde et iusto opere speraverunt in eo, qui rex est regum et dominus dominancium in secula seculorum. Amen.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit prologus libri celestis imperatoris ad reges.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f. 252rb\endash 255ra) Table of Contents cap. I\endash LVII. (f. 255ra) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit liber celestis imperatoris ad reges revelatus divinitus beate Birgitte, principisse Nerecie de regno Suecie. Summus imperator Christus loquitur per sponsam ad reges ostendens se esse verum omnium creatorem et regem in trinitate et unitate regnantem et dicit, qualiter mundum ordinavit regendum duplici potestate, scilicet ecclesiastica et laycali, que in apostolis sanctis Petro et Paulo principaliter designantur. Capitulum primum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < Notiz am unteren Rand: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Nota quod iste liber celestius imperatoris ad reges est octavus et ultimus liber in ordine istorum librorum celestium.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 255rb) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Vidi palacium grande de inconprehensibile in magnitudine simile celo sereno, in quo erant innumerabiles persone sedentes in sedibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 celebrando missam de sancta trinitate et colligant pauperes laudentque humiliter pedes eorum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  Ed.: Book 8: Hans Aili (ed.), Sancta Birgitta. Revelaciones. Book VIII, Stockholm 2002; text of the prologue according to the edition of Arne J\u246 \'f6nsson, Alfonso of Ja\u233 \'e9n. His Life and Works with Critical Editions of the \ldblquote Epistola Solitarii\rdblquote , the \ldblquote Informaciones\rdblquote  and the \ldblquote Epistola Serui Christi\rdblquote , Lund 1989 (Studia Graeca et Latina Lundensia 1), pp. 117\endash 171. CALMA Bd. 2,4, p. 410 f., no. 1. Ulrich Montag, Birgitta von Schweden, in: Verfasserlexikon, vol. 1, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1978, col. 867\endash 869, here col. 868 f., and vol. 11, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 2004, col. 258. For Alphonsus Giennensis see CALMA vol. 1,2, p. 189, ALPH 23, no. 4.]}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f2\fnil\fcharset161 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red153\green0\blue204;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [K. S.: ff. 304va\endash 310vb \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Birgitta Suecica: Orationes\plain \f2\lang1032\fs26  (version \u916 \'c4).\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  Oratio 1: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hec oracio fuit a deo revelata beate Birgitte in qua devote et pulchre laudatur gloriosa virgo Maria\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f.\~304vb) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 de sancta concepcione et infancia sua et de omnibus virtuosis actibus et laboribus et magnis doloribus tocius vite sue et de sanctissima morte et assumpcione sua.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Benedicta et venerabilis sis tu, domina mea, virgo Maria, dei mater sanctissima et cuius vere tu es optima creatura\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85; (f. 304v) note in the lower margin: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Nota quod oracio de passione Christi et de vita et laude virginis Maria omne \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [?] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 agitur in legenda sancte Birgitte in prima parte, capitulo viii\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 o\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 . Est divisa in quatuor partes ut hic sequitur prima: Benedicta et venerabilis sis tu domina mea, virgo Maria, secunda: Benedictus sis tu domine mi, deus meus et amor meus, tercia: Domine mi, Ihesu Christe, quarta: O domina mea, regina celi, mater dei etc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ; (f. 306va) Oratio 2: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hec oracio fuit a deo revelata beate Birgitte. In qua pulchre ac devote laudatur Christus cum narracione seriosa de sua gloriosa incarnacione et de omnibus actibus et laboribus et doloribus vite et sanctissime mortis sue et de ascensione in celum et missione spiritus sancti in discipulos et cetera.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Benedictus sis tu, domine mi, deus meus et amor meus, dilectissime anime mee, qui es unus deus in tribus personis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85; (f.\~308ra) Oratio 3: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 In hac oracione a deo revelata beate Birgitte satis pulchre laudantur omnia membra sanctissimi corporis domini nostri Ihesu Christi et eciam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f.\~308rb) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 virtuosissimi eius corporis actus singillatim per ordinem.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Domine mi Ihesu Christe, quamvis ego bene scio, quod benedictum corpus tuum incessanter laudatur et glorificatur armonia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85; (f. 309va) Oratio 4: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 In ista oracione, que divinitus fuit revelata beate Birgitte, devotissime et pulchre laudantur omnia membra gloriosi corporis virginis Marie et virtuosi actus eius corporales.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 O domina mea, vita mea, regina celi, mater dei, quamvis ego certa sum, quod tuum corpus gloriosum a tota celesti curea \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  cum canore iubilo incessanter laudatur in celis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 atque pro hiis, qui in purgatorio per eam adiutorium et salamen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  habuerunt, qui vivis et regnas cum patre et spiritu sancto in secula seculorum. Amen.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit liber celestis imperatoris ad reges beate Birgitte, principisse de regno Suecie, divinitus revelatus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \endash  Ed.: Sten Eklund (ed.), Sancta Birgitta. Opera minora 3: Quattuor oraciones, Stockholm 1991, pp. 65\endash 92 (MS mentioned p. 10). Ulrich Montag, Birgitta von Schweden, in: Verfasserlexikon, vol. 1, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1978, col. 867\endash 869, and vol. 11, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 2004, col. 258. CALMA vol. 2,4, p. 411, no. 4.]}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f2\fnil\fcharset161 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red153\green0\blue204;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [K. S.: ff. 310vb\endash 398vb \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Birgitta Suecica: Revelationes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Liber 6\endash 7. (f. 310vb\endash 375va) Liber 6. (f. 310vb\endash 315va) Table of Contents cap. I\endash CIX. (f. 315va) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit liber sextus celestis revelacionum beate Birgitte, principisse der regno Suecie, divinitus revelatus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 315vb) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Verba matris dei ad sponsam narrancia pulchritudinem Christi et qualiter frequenter Judei in aliquo agone cordis positi ibant ad inspiciendum vultum eius et consolabantur. Capitulum I.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Mater dei loquebatur ad sponsam dicens: Ego sum regina celi. Filius meus diligit te toto corde; ideo consulo tibi, ut nichil diligas nisi ipsum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ideo dimittatur proprie voluntati, quia deo accepcius est in mundo iuste vivere et laborare manibus quam in heremo vel religione stare sine caritate dei.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit liber sexta celestis revelacionum dei beate Birgitte, principisse de regno Suecie, divinitus revelatus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f. 375va\endash 398vb) Liber 7. (f. 375va\endash 377rb) Table of Contents cap. I\endash XXXII. (f. 377v) Note in margin: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Item nota, quod iste liber ultimus potest et esse septimus in ordine etc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < (f. 377va) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit liber ultimus celestis revelacionum dei beate Birgitte, principisse de regno Suecie, divinitus revelatus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Revelacio, quam habuit domina Birgitta in Roma post annum iubelei, in qua virgo Maria prenunciat ei, quod itura esset Iherusalem et Bethleem, quando placuerit deo, promictens ei sibi tunc ostendere modum, quo ipsa peperit filium suum benedictum. Capitulum primum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Cum esset in Roma beata domina Birgitta sponsa Christi et quadam vice oracioni vacaret, cepit cogitare de partu virginis et de illa summa bonitate dei\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 cum maxima devocione et reverencia inter manus predictarum personarum emisit spiritum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit liber ultimus celestis revelacionum dei beate Birgitte principisse Nerecie de regno Suecie divinitus revelatus. Deo gracias.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \endash  [K. S.: Ed.: Book 6: Birger Bergh (ed.), Sancta Birgitta. Revelaciones. Book VI, Stockholm 1991; Book 7: Birger Bergh (ed.), Den heliga Birgittas Revelaciones. Bok VII, Uppsala 1967 (MS is divided in 32 chapters; MS mentioned p. 41). Ulrich Montag, Birgitta von Schweden, in: Verfasserlexikon, vol. 1, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1978, col. 867\endash 869, here col. 868 f., and vol. 11, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 2004, col. 258. CALMA vol. 2,4, p. 410 f., no. 1.]}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f2\fnil\fcharset161 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red153\green0\blue204;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 399ra\endash 400ra \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Vita s. Birgittae Suecicae,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  in German. >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit vita beate Birgitte in teutonico sub brevitate conpilata.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Sancta Birgitta ist geboren von den konigklichem stamme von gotlant vnd ist gewest eyn eliche frauwe her Vlfon von Vlfason, eyn forst des landes in dem konigklichem von suueden \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 also dut er noch\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (f. 400ra) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 degelich nach irem dode an manchem enden in mancherhande wonder wercken von czeichen.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  Ed.: Carl Selmer, Die sp\u228 \'e4tmittelhochdeutschen Bestandteile der\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 lateinischen Birgitta-Handschrift der Universit\u228 \'e4tsbibliothek zu Yale und ihre Dialektbestimmung, in: Publications of the Modern Language Association 51 (1936), pp. 37\endash 58, here pp. 38\endash 40. [K. S.: Undhagen, Sancta Birgitta. Revelaciones. Book I, see above, p.\~179, n.\~6. Montag, Das Werk der heiligen Birgitta, see above, p. 40 (MS mentioned); Ulrich Montag, Birgitta von Schweden, in: Verfasserlexikon, vol. 1, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1978, col. 867\endash 869, here col. 869, and vol. 11, Berlin \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 2004, col. 258.]}

