\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Written in Northern Germany or Denmark in the late 16th century, after 1565; perhaps copied by Pawel Hansen whose signature appears on ff. 154r, 178r (The copy seems to have been made all at one time, not in separate sections as the laws were decreed.). Early provenance unknown. Sold by Weigel (Leipzig, 1881; note on original front flyleaf) to comte Paul Riant (bookplate, and monogram on spine; L. de German and L. Polain, Catalogue de la Biblioth\u232 \'e8que de feu M. le comte Riant, Paris 1896, v. 1, p. 362, no. 2487), whose Scandinavian library was given to Yale in 1896 by Mrs. Henry Farnam.}

