\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Written in Germany in the late 16th or early 17th century; inscription at top of f. 1r: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Ex b. viri Andr. Schotti Scabini Gedanensis bibliotheca publica auctionis lege\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [\u8230 \'85] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 dita hic codex supperlectili librariae adjectus est Joachimi Guilielmi Weickhmann Ged. 1764\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 . On the third flyleaf at the front: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Chronique de Pom\u233 \'e9ranie ecrite en 1570 par Valentin de Eickstetten, Chancellier des Princes de Pom\u233 \'e9ranie. Un abr\u233 \'e9g\u233 \'e9 en a \u233 \'e9t\u233 \'e9 fait en 1728 et imprim\u233 \'e9 par Balthazar \u224 \'e0 Gryphiswold in 8\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 o\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 . Belonged to Comte Paul Riant (bookplate inside front cover; apparently not listed in L. Germon and L. Polain, Catalogue de la Biblioth\u232 \'e8que de feu M. le comte Riant, Paris 1896, p. 361\endash 362, no. 2486). Given to Yale in 1896 by Mrs. Henry Farnam.}

