\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 459v\endash 524v \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Daniel Cramer, Funeral orations for the Dukes of Pomerania\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , in Latin. Colorful and elaborate title page occupies ff. 459v\endash 460r, written sidewise: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ex mandato illustrissimi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 principis ac domini domini casimiri ducis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  parentalia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 posthuma \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  celebrabit Daniel Cramerus, D. Pastor\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Text: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Si quas mihi hoc ipso die dicendi partes necessitas imperauit \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 notisque nostris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [crossed out: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 annis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (?)] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 annuit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Christus Jesus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 benedictus in aeternum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dixi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< \endash  Daniel Cramer (1568\endash 1637), Lutheran theologian and archdeacon of Stettin (cf. Allgemeine Deutsche Biographie, v. 4, pp. 546\endash 547, and H. Heyden, Pommersche Geistliche vom Mittelalter bis zum 19. Jahrhundert, in: Ver\u246 \'f6ffentlichungen der historischen Kommission f\u252 \'fcr Pommern 11, Cologne 1965, pp. 173\endash 179.}

