{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Paper (watermarks similar to Briquet Armoiries 1656) and parchment for leaves heavily illuminated, ff. ii (original paper, i verso and ii recto ruled in ink for 19 lines, but blank) + 376 + iv (original paper), 131 x 102 (93 x 61) mm., trimmed. Written in 20 long lines; single vertical and double horizontal bounding lines, full across. Ruled faintly in lead; a few prickings along outer edge.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 Two original paper fly-leaves, connected to original parchment pastedown; I\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , II\endash IV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , V\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\endash 4, following f. 40), VI\endash XI\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , XII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , XIII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , XIV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\endash 8, following f. 116), XV\endash XXI\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , XXII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\endash 1, following f. 186), XXIII\endash XXVI\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , XXVII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , XXVIII\endash XXX\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , XXXI\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\endash 1, 10, following folios 253 and 261), XXXII\endash XXXIV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , XXXV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , XXXVI\endash XLIV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , XLV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\endash 1, following f. 367), four original paper fly-leaves connected to original parchment paste-down.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 Text written in varying bookhands, most with b\u226 \'e2tarde influence; more formal scripts for some rubrics and portions of text on parchment.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 Two historiated initials, 12- and 10-line, on parchment bifolios: f. 15r (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Primo nocturno\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) Mary as child before altar, and f. 84v (Prayer to the Virgin) Kneeling angel with harp, the letters gold and blue with brown and red penwork, the figures crudely drawn in pen and colored brown, blue and green, against bright red grounds with white highlights; brown and red calligraphic flourishes with red, green, blue and yellow dots extending along upper and side edges of written space. 12-, 10-, and 9-line initials (ff. 13r, 96r, 115r, 179r, 222r, 258r, 322v) gold (or red for ff. 258r, 322v) and blue, filled with brown floral penwork designs with calligraphic flourishes and dots, as above. Floral borders for each 12- through 9-line initial (except ff. 15r and 258r), red, blue, and green flowers with gold dot centers, connected by brown ink stems, arranged in rows or spirals; ff. 13r and 84v with a vase and bird in the margins. Two 9-line initials, ff. 274r and 298r, on parchment bifolios, in a markedly different style, green and blue respectively, with yellow and white highlights, against gold grounds, filled on f. 274r with a large flower, blue and red, on f. 298r with short sections of curling pink and green acanthus. Borders large blue or red flowers with gold dots and centers or short sections of blue and red acanthus on spiraling brown stems with small green teardrop leaves. Numerous 7- through 2-line initials, red and/or blue, with brown penwork and flourishes, as above. I-initials, up to 13-line, red or blue throughout. Some capital W's in text in blue or red. 2-line KL monograms, alternating red and blue. Some portions of the text, including proper names, underlined in red. Notes for rubricator in gutter, perpendicular to text.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Written in Cologne/Lower Rhine (Ripuarian language area) in the second half of the 15th century for Augustinian use (see ff. 1r\endash 12v); early provenance otherwise unknown. Belonged to Henri-Auguste Br\u246 \'f6lemann (bookplate inside front cover; polygonal label, white with blue edging and \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 A N\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 o\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  212/9x1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  inside back cover); collection formed during the early part of the 19th century by Br\u246 \'f6lemann and sold by order of his great grand-daughter Madame Etienne Mallett (Sotheby's, 4\endash 5 May l926, no. 175). Booktag of the bookseller Menno Hertzberger of Amsterdam. Acquired by Henry Fletcher and presented to Yale in 1955 by Mrs. Henry Fletcher.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Faye and Bond, p. 39, no. 196.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Binding: s. xvi. Original sewing on four supports attached to wooden boards. Covered in dark brown calf with corner turn-in tongues. Blind-tooled with concentric borders, an X, roses and small flowers in the central panel, roses and rampant lions in the outer borders. Two clasp-and-catch fastenings, the catch on the upper board. Rebacked and the endbands probably added. Straps replaced. Covers lined with fragments of unidentified scientific text, in Latin (s. XV).}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

