{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Parchment, ff. i (contemporary parchment) + 138, 165 x 120 (108 x 78) mm. Written in ca. 17 long lines; single vertical bounding lines, widely spaced double upper and lower horizontal bounding lines and two additional rulings in upper margin for running titles (ff. 63v\endash 138v), all full across; ruled in ink. Prickings in upper margin.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 I\endash XVII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , XVIII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 . Catchwords along lower edge near gutter.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 Written by a single scribe in well formed gothic textura. ff. 1r\endash 62r, 113v\endash 119r, and 132r\endash 134v have 4-line staves, in red, and black square notes.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 Uninspired blue initial, 2-stave, on f. 1r, infilled and surrounded by red penwork flourishes with blue accents. Similar plain initials, 2-line, alternate in blue, red, and black with red throughout. Running titles and headings in red.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Written apparently in Southern Germany as a gift for Barbara Pfintzing, who entered a nunnery in 1441 at the age of 16; inscription on f. i verso: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Item ich swester barbara pfinczingin w\u252 \'fcrd geporn noch unsers lieben herren ihesu christi gepurt. M. CCCC. und in dem xxv Iar am achten tag vor weihen nahten. Vnd kom in das kloster an sant Erharsz tag. M. CCCC. und in dem xlj iar\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 . The text (see ff. 1r\endash 62v and ff. 76v\endash 84r) indicates that the manuscript was produced for use in a Dominican house of nuns; liturgical directions are written in German (the feminine forms in the antiphons and prayers often bear suprascript masculine endings, in red). Acquired by Henry Fletcher from Dawson's Book Shop, Los Angeles; gift of Mrs. Henry Fletcher in 1953.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 secundo folio: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 dicens ite}

