\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 133v\endash 140v \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Honorius of Autun\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 , \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Elucidarius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 excerpts. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Quid est predestinatio. predestinatio est ea ordinatio que ante creatum seculum quosdam ad suum regnum preordinauit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... f. 139v, mid-page: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Scriptum est pater non portabit iniquitatem filii nec filius patris. Si filii parentibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 //; text continues without a break on f. 139v: //\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 leti sunt. De absentibus amicis solliciti. Cum autem omnes simul ueniunt amplius gaudebunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... (f. 140v) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Si autem uelociter contigerit pro alterius sancti merito fit ut sancto Mart\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 //; text completed in another hand, s. XV ?: //\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ino episcopo anima latronis apparuit cuius altare destruxit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Two excerpts from the Elucidarius attributed to Honorius of Autun, Book II.28\endash 45 and Book III.27\endash 30; PL 172, col. 1109\endash 1176. See Y. Lef\u232 \'e8vre, L'Elucidarium et les lucidaires (Biblioth\u232 \'e8que des \u201 \'c9coles Fran\u231 \'e7aises d'Ath\u232 \'e8nes et de Rome 180), Paris 1954. Ultra-violet photography has revealed that the passage from Book III originally continued on f. 107rv with the words \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 anima latronis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  and continued through III.32. The passage probably was erased after the manuscript was misbound (see physical description).}

