\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 189r\endash 190r \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Bonaventure, Itinerarium mentis ad deum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , chapters 5.4\endash 5 and 8.4, excerpts. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Vnde uerissime apparet quod sicut oculus uespertilionis se habet ad lucem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 uide ergo ipsum purissimum esse si potes et occurret tibi quod ipsum non potest cogitari. ut ab alio acceptum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (f. 189r) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dicendo cum dyonysio ad deum trinitatem.  summitas superessentialis et superdeus superoptime christianorum inspector\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Benedictus dominus in eternum et dicet omnis populus fiat fiat amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (f. 190r) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Pseudo-Dionysius, De mystica theologia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , paraphrase of chapter 1.1. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 O herte vrunt timothee wachte dat niemen ongeleerde dese dincen hore\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 o herre leid ons in dat heimeliche verborgen onbekinte clare stilnisse der lutren gemoude di ougen nies\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [?] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 en hant\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [to which is added, in the same hand:] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Animalia sancta ambulabant ante facies eorum vbi erat impetus spiritus illic et ambulabant\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . ff. 190v\endash 192v blank. \endash  Two abridged excerpts from Bonaventure, Itinerarium mentis ad deum, chapters 5.4\endash 5 and 8.4, to which has been added a paraphrase of the Pseudo-Dionysius, De mystica theologia, chapter 1.1, in Low German. The compiler recognized that the second excerpt from the Itinerarium is itself a paraphrase of chapter 1.1 of the De mystica theologia. No complete Low German translation of De mystica theologia is known. Another, non-identical Low German paraphrase of chapter 1.1 occurs in a Sammelhandschrift in Kloster Ebstorf (Niedersachsen), MS IV, 12, ff. 297v\endash 298v, for which see W. Stammler, Meister Eckhart in Norddeutschland, in: Zeitschrift f\u252 \'fcr deutsches Altertum 59, N. F. 47 (1922), p. 206. All three passages added, s. XIV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , on folios originally left blank. ff. 190v\endash 192v blank.}

