\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 1r\endash 2v [\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Ps.-Bernardus Claraevallensis: Rhythmica oratio ad membra Christi\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (Ad manus, Ad latus, Ad pectus, Ad cor)]. \u9553 \'a6\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ad manus. / Salve salve, Iesu bone / fatigatus in agone\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 paratus gratis omnibus. / Ecce me tibi pre\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sento\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ]\u9553 \'a6 \endash  The lower margin has been trimmed with the loss of the bottom two lines of text. (f. 1v) \u9553 \'a6\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 qui presto es amantibus / In hac cruce sic extensus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 me defendant, Iesu Christe nunc et / in extremis periculis. / Ad latus. Salve, salve, summe bonus / ad parcendum nimis pronus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quam acerbe sunt distenta / mara crucis torrida. / Salve, latus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u9553 \'a6 \endash  The lower margin has been trimmed with the loss of the bottom two lines of text. (f. 2r) \u9553 \'a6 [faded: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 scatet fons cruoris / qui corda lavat\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  sordida. / Ecce tibi appropinquo\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 tuo victus ex amore / mori posset pre \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (f. 2v) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 amore / te unum amans unice \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sed apud te permaneat. / Ad pectus. / Salve, salus mea Deus / Iesu dulcis amor meus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  pax et pausa fatigatis / humilium triclinium. / Ad cor. / Summi regis cor, aveto / te saluto corde leto\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ut te nobis impartires / ut\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u9553 \'a6 \endash  Print: PL 184, col. 1321\endash 1322. [K. S.: Walther, Initia no. 17126. See Franz Xaver Haimerl, Mittelalterliche Fr\u246 \'f6mmigkeit im Spiegel der Gebetbuchliteratur S\u252 \'fcddeutschlands (M\u252 \'fcnchener theologische Studien I, 4), M\u252 \'fcnchen 1952, p. 66, n. 340; p. 78, n. 443; p. 81, n. 469; p. 93; p. 98, n. 579; p. 104, n. 609; p. 109, n. 627.]}

