\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Parchment   \u183 \'b7   4 folios (fols. 1 and 4 and fols. 2 and 3 form bifolia)   \u183 \'b7   Fol. 1 measures 171 x 121 mm; fol. 2 measures 134 x 125 mm; fol. 3, 134 x 75 mm; fol. 4, 172 x 76 mm (written space 132 x 95 mm)   \u183 \'b7   1 column   \u183 \'b7   36 lines. Ruled in ink. Pricking in outer margin   \u183 \'b7   Written in gothic script (littera textualis)   \u183 \'b7   3-line initials at the beginning of chapters are in red and are not set apart from the text. 1-line initials are in black, highlighted with red, and are not set apart from the text. Rubrics are written in red in the same script as the text. Punctuation consists of the punctus and the virgule   \u183 \'b7   Contemporary (or slightly later) page numbers in Roman numerals in the upper margins of ff. 1r, 2r and 4r identify them as pp. 14, 16 and 20 of the manuscript. The folio number on f. 3r (originally p. 18) has been cut away. This numbering is consistent with the length of the work. The B\u252 \'fcchlein would have filled around 60 folios.}

