\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 f. 11v \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 23 verses\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  dealing with the numerical value of the letters of the alphabet. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Nota bene. Possidet A numero quingentos ordine recto,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  / \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Trecentos quoque B per se retinere videtur;\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  / \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Non plus quam centum C littera fertur habere,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  / \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Littera D velud A quingentos significabit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Y dat centenos et quinquaginta tenendos,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  / \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ultima Z canit finem, bis mille tenebit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Walther, Initia 14298. Walther does not mention an author, but they are said to be excerpted from Hugutio of Pisa (d. 1212), Liber derivationum.}

