\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 62r\endash 70r \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Mundinus de Luzzi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (?), \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Synonyma medicinae Synonima Mundini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Albula. Argiofora. Argiofea gemma. Argyofea margarita\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Zucara roseta. Zuccus rosarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Expliciunt synonima Mundini que sunt necessaria apotecariis et quibusdam aliis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Finito libro sit laus et gloria Christo. Amen dicamus, semper cum Deo maneamus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Synonyma medicinae\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  here ascribed to Mondino de\rquote  Luzzi (Mundinus de Luzzi, d. 1326 ?). Thorndike and Kibre 75. Written on 3\endash 5 columns per page, the columns numbered in the upper margin by means of series of alphabets; the lemmata within each alphabetical section by means of red arabic numerals. ff. 70v\endash 73v blank.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 74r\endash 80v \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Synonyma medicinae\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Alhasel, id est puncti rubri qui sunt ut pulicis morsus, et fiunt in omnibus membris et precipue in oculis, et cito recedunt: infirmitas oculorum ut pruritus in oculis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [added:] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 s. die r\u246 \'f6thel. Algocodie, id est nodi qui sunt in collo et gula\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Zinzibratum. Zinziber conditum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (f. 80v) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \u167 \'a7 Oliatham ist clain weys weyrauch. Diabotes morbus est vesice, scilicet quando urina retinere non potest\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Oxiteotheum est emplastrum valens ossibus confractis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Thorndike and Kibre 73, 80, 95. Alphabetical list written in three columns a page, occasionally with German translations, followed by some additions in Latin and in German. The groups of lemmata are numbered by means of letters.}

