\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ff. 81r\endash 83r \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Aegidius Corboliensis (?),\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 De urinis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipiunt versus Egidii physici de consideracione urinarum. Panditur urine color hec artis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [?] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 medicine\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Sunt gemini pulsus formicans vermicularum Certi precones mortis redolentque sepulcrum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  De urinis, here ascribed to Giles of Corbeil (Aegidius Corboliensis, d. 1224 ?), but according to Thorndike and Kibre 422 the latter\rquote s book has a different incipit. J. L. Choulant, ed., Aegidii Corboliensis carmina medica, Leipzig 1826, pp. ?? This text is followed by other medical verses.}

