\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\qc\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 III
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\qc\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ff. 161\endash 261. Paper, 290 x 210 mm. Watermarks: column var. Briquet 4408 (?); bull\rquote s head var. Briquet 14825 (?) (last three folios). Narrow parchment stays in the middle of the quires. Some leaves torn or damaged by moist; ff. 169\endash 170 badly damaged   \u183 \'b7   XV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 161\endash 172), XVI\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 16\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 173\endash 188), XVII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\endash 3, ff. 189\endash 199), XVIII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 200\endash 211), XIX\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\endash 6, ff. 212\endash 222), XX\endash XXII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 223\endash 258), XXIII (three singletons, ff. 259\endash 261)   \u183 \'b7   Frame-ruling for two columns of 26\endash 37 lines. On ff. 162r\endash 237r the ruling is traced in brown ink (210 x 150 mm., intercolumnar space 20 mm.; ff. 238r\endash 261v traced in lead (210 x 160 mm., intercolumnar space 14 mm.)   \u183 \'b7   ff. 162r\endash 237r were apparently copied by three hands: A (ff. 162r\endash 170v, 172r\endash 173rb1, 175r\endash 187v), B (ff. 171rv, 173rb1\endash 174v), C (ff. 189r\endash 237r). ff. 238r\endash 261v were copied by two resembling hands. All write Gothica Cursiva Libraria   \u183 \'b7   The decoration on ff. 162r\endash 237r consists of 3\endash 4 line plain initials in red; at the opening a 5-line flourished initial in red. ff. 238r\endash 259v have red stroking of the opening majuscules of all verses and 2-line plain red initials. On ff. 260r\endash 261v the majuscules are heightened with red. The Fables on ff. 162r\endash 237r are illustrated with unframed watercoloured pen drawings, with the following subjects: ff. 163r: Fox and Raven (I.1); 164r: Eagle and Sun (I.2); 164v: Raven, Fox and Ape (I.3); 165v: Cicada (bird) and Ant (I.4); 167r: Raven and Fox (I.5); 168r: Spider and Fly (I.6); 169r: Mouse and Tortoise in front of a house (I.7); 169v: Fish and Fisherman in sailing boat (I.8); 171r: Fox and Ape pointing to moon (I.9); 172r: Ant and Fox (I.10); 174r: Ox and Hog (I.11); 175r: Horse and Ox under a tree (I.12); 176r: Raven and three Hens (I.13); 176v: Fox dressed as a priest and reading book, and Cock (I.13); 177v: Ox and Wolf (I.14); 179r: Raven and Frog (I.15); 180r: Ass and Lion (I.16); 181r: Sun and Mercury (I.17); 182r: Fox, Mouse and Lion (I.18); 183v: Viper and Porcupine (I.19); 185r: Raven and Dove (I.20); 186v: Grain and Stones (I.21); 189r: Bear attacking Lamb, Dove (I.22); 190v: Wolf and Adder (I.23); 191r: Wolf as pilgrim, with Dog, Bear, Wild Ass and Lion (I.24); 191v: Peacock, Wolf and Hog (I.24); 192r: Raven, Unicorn (= Panther), Ape, Boar, Lamb, Hare, Porcupine and Ox, on a hill (I.24); 193r: Crowned Lady (= Nature) holding Eye and Ear (I.25); 194r: Four Stones in the earth (I.26); 195v: Five Trees (I.27); 196v: Earth and Air (II.1); 197v: Dead Man (= Body) and Soul (II.2); 198r: Goat at a fountain (II.3); 198v: Porcupine (II.3); 200r: Ostrich, Hen and four flying Birds (II.4); 201r: Horse, Man in armour with Sword, Mule (II.5); 202r: Sailor in a ship, Raven, crowned Ape on throne holding sceptre, and Fox (II.6); 203r: Hare and Sparrow (II.7; in the original: Bee and Sparrow); 205r: Man and Woman (= Will and Reason) discussing (II.8); 206r: Sheep and Stag (II.9); 208r: two Women (Feeling and Intellect) discussing in front of a hilltop castle (II.10); 209r: Bear in lair, Fox, Hind and Stag (II.11); 210r: Stag and Hind (II.11); 211r: Cloud and Earth (II.12); 213r: winged Ant and Nightingale in tree (II.13); 214r: Reed and Sugar-Cane (II.14); 215r: Cock and Fox with tree (II.15); 217r: Toothed Fish and Swordfish (II.17); 218v: Rhinoceros and Raven (II.18); 220r: two Mules (II.19); 221r: Duck, two Hens, Fox and Ape (II.20); 222r: Peacock and Porcupine (II.21); 224r: Ostrich, Peacock, four flying Birds (II.22); 225r: Thorn-Bush and Fig-Tree (II.23); 226r: Saturn (unfinished, II.24); 227v: Raven and Peacock (II.25); 228v: Nightingale in cage and Raven (II.26); 229v: Raven and Fox, with tree (II.27); 231r: Cock and Raven (II.28); 232r: Ape and Wild Ass (II.29); 234r: Dove in Mud (II.30); 235r: Raven and Fox (III.1); 236r: Mole (III.2); 237r: Snake (= Crocodile) and Bird (= Scrophilus, III.3).}

