\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Paper, ff. 174, 295 x 220 mm. Watermarks: var. Piccard, v. 15, VIII.1547 (?); var. Piccard, v. 110, III.1667 (?). Original alpha-numerical system of foliation in red ink on ff. 10r\endash 172v, in the middle of the upper margin of the recto pages, beginning f. 10r: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 A I\endash A X\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 B I\endash B X\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , etc. up to \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 R VI\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (= f. 172r). Two folios, with early foliation \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 P IV\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  and \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 P V\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , are missing between ff. 151 and 152. Errors in the original foliation: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 A III\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  is followed by \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 A V\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 12\endash 13); \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 N VIII\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  is followed by \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 N X\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 136\endash 137); ff. 152 and 153 are both foliated \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 P VII\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (f. 152 should be \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 P VI\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ). In the s. XVII foliation f. 142 (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 O V\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) is erroneously followed by f. 144 (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 O VI\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ). Badly damaged by the acid ink, especially ff. 73\endash 120 (quires VII\endash X). The quires are strengthened by means of parchment stays (see Binding)   \u183 \'b7   I\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (+ 1 singleton, f. 13; ff. 1\endash 13), II\endash V\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 14\endash 61), VI\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\endash 1, no loss of text; ff. 62\endash 72), VII\endash XII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 73\endash 145), XIII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\endash 7, \endash 8; ff. 146\endash 155), XIV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 156\endash 167), XV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\endash 8, \endash 9, \endash 10; ff. 168\endash 174). Horizontal catchwords near the fold, several ones lost partly or entirely at the trimming of the codex. In the lower margin of f. 120v, above the catchword of quire X, a contemporary hand has written in green ink \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 schaw auff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22    \u183 \'b7   Frame-ruling in brown ink for two columns of c. 30 lines, c. 221 x c. 142 mm., intercolumnar space 18 mm   \u183 \'b7   Copied in 1462 by Johannes Geratwol in Gothica Cursiva Libraria/Currens with some Bastarda characteristics. Rear pastedown is added in Gothica Hybrida Libraria under Humanistic influence   \u183 \'b7   ff. 1r\endash 172v have headings, heightening of the majuscules and mostly 1-line plain initials in red or green. The initial on f. 1r has green penwork. The first lines of all titles on ff. 1r\endash 9v are underlined in red.}

