{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Parchment, ff. II + 65, 200 x 135 mm.; ff. 62\endash 63 inserted on paper   \u183 \'b7   I\endash VI\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 (ff. 1\endash 48), VII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 6 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 (ff. 49\endash 54), VIII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 8\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 55\endash 61, ff. 64\endash 65)   \u183 \'b7   The main section of the manuscript (ff. 1r\endash 61v) has pricking in the upper, outer and lower margins and ruling in black ink for one column of 30 lines below top line, 148 x 100 mm. Ruling type 36 with a wide distance between the double vertical bounding lines. The last but one prick in the vertical row is double. In the Calendar (ff. 1r\endash 61v) there are 6 days on every page, providing 5 lines for entering obits every day. There are many blank spaces and days without obits   \u183 \'b7   Many Gothic hands ranging from the early sixteenth to the nineteenth centuries, but mostly from the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries. The Calendar itself (ff. 1r\endash 61v) is written in Gothica Textualis Formata in red ink; f. 61v too is in Textualis Formata. f. 1v and Iv are copied by Sister Eve Welschpilch in Gothica Hybrida Libraria/Formata. It was apparently the same scribe who entered the earliest obits in the Obituary   \u183 \'b7   The Day Letters are in red (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 A\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) or stroked with red (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 B\endash G\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ). Names of months and feasts in red.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 The Obituary (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Seleboich\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , see f. 1v) was organized in the early sixteenth century, obits being transcribed from a s. XV manuscript recording the deaths of members and benefactors; the majority of the obits was entered afterwards at the time of the decease of the persons involved. That the Convent to which it belonged was that of the Poor Clares in Trier appears from ff. 62r\endash 63v; its patronym \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Sta. Maria Magdalena\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  is mentioned in one of the printed documents kept together with the manuscript. The archival number \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 No. I\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (s. XVIII) is written in the upper margin of f. 1v. Presented c. 1860 by Dr. John Schu\u233 \'e9, Hartford, to the Connecticut Historical Society (bookplate of the latter, with motto \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Sustinet qui transtulit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , pasted on the rear pastedown). Purchased from Laurence Witten, Southport, Connecticut on the Edwin J. Beinecke Fund.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 Original binding: brown blind-tooled leather over oak boards, decorated with double fillets and small lozenge tools (\ldblquote Ihesus\rdblquote  and \ldblquote Maria\rdblquote  monograms) and rosettes; bound on five white leather thongs. Spine with five raised bands, rebacked. Remnants of one brass clasp attached to the rear cover. The front pastedown is detached.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 f. Av \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Note by Sister Eve Welschpilch\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , 23 June 1536, about the way of lightening the burden of commemorations (vigils) conceded to the Convent by the Provincial of the Order, Matthias Weynssen of Dordrecht, on 29 June 1522. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 It is tzo wissen, in den jaren unssers Herren XVc XXII, Peter und Paulus dach, umm den g\u246 \'f6tlichen dienst und gezijde die vollenk\u246 \'f6melicher zo halden und darna beiden vur unse noitdurfft, hait unsser erewirdigster provinciail minster Mathias Weynssen von Dordrach, in und anbrengen der zweyher andechtiger wirdiger unsre\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (...) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 vaeder, pater Jacob Vanckel und broder Hermannus Molite, uns verlycht und absolviert van den vyl jairgetze vigilien vur die doden, besonder die men so vyl jair her halden hait\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Geschreben in profesto sancti Iohannis Baptiste anno Domini XVc XXXVI. Eyn Ave Maria vur die schryber suster Eva Welschpilch\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  See also ff. 62r\endash 63v. This text is no longer present. f. Ar blank.}

