\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 [K. S.: restored]   \u183 \'b7   Paper (f. 1 parchment), ff. I (paper) + 168 + I (paper), 150 x 105 mm. 4\u176 \'b0 folding. Parchment stays in the centre of the quires   \u183 \'b7   [K. S.: six watermarks: bull\rquote s head (Ochsenkopf): watermark twins (O1 and O2): Ochsenkopf (O1): very similar WZIS DE0480-PO-62588 (1474, Augsburg), very similar WZIS DE0480-PO-62589 (1474, Augsburg), ~\~(similar) WZIS DE8085-PO-62579 (1471, Ellwangen), ~\~(similar) WZIS DE8085-PO-62571 (1471, o. O.) and Ochsenkopf (O2): very similar WZIS DE8085-PO-62298 (1471, Ellwangen), ~\~(similar) WZIS DE8370-PO-62303 (1473, Ulm); crown with arch (Krone mit B\u252 \'fcgel K1): very similar WZIS DE8310-Mc103_70 (um 1473/1482), very similar WZIS DE8310-Mc103_89 (um 1473/1482); mount of five coupeaux (F\u252 \'fcnfberg F1): =\~WZIS AT8100-PO-154285 (Augsburg, 1474), =\~WZIS DE6405-PO-154288 (1476, Ansbach); bull\rquote s head (Ochsenkopf): watermark twins (O3 and O4): Ochsenkopf (O3): =\~WZIS DE8085-PO-60258 (1475, o. O.), =\~WZIS DE8085-PO-60266 (1476, o. O.), =\~WZIS DE6300-PO-60265 (1476, Ellwangen), =\~WZIS DE8085-PO-60263 (1476, Stuttgart) and Ochsenkopf (O4): =\~WZIS DE8085-PO-58941 (1475, Urach), =\~WZIS DE8085-PO-58949 (1476, Konstanz), =\~WZIS DE8085-PO-58950 (1476, Konstanz)]   \u183 \'b7   I\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 1\endash 12; the first paper leaf has been replaced by a parchment leaf), II\endash XIV\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 12\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (ff. 13\endash 168) [K. S.: quire formula: 14 VI\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 168\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ]   \u183 \'b7   Horizontal catchwords at right, missing on f. 72v (quire VI). [K. S.: The catchword \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 end vnd nach\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (crossed out) on fol. 168v implies that the manuscript is incomplete; quire signatures partly cut off: quire I: [\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ]\endash \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 9\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ; further quires: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 1\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 \endash \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 6\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ; the last three quires without quire signatures]   \u183 \'b7   with modern pencil foliation (\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 5\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  10\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  15 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 30\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  40\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 165\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 )]   \u183 \'b7   Almost invisible blind frame ruling for one column, 14\endash 16 lines (mostly 15), c. 90 x c. 58 mm   \u183 \'b7   Two scribes: A, called \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 S. Bawman\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (Baumann, f. 140v, see above), from N\u246 \'f6rdlingen (Bavaria), writes Gothica Hybrida Libraria/Formata with calligraphic extensions on the top and bottom lines (ff. 2r\endash 140v); B writes Gothica Cursiva Libraria/Currens (ff. 141r\endash 168v)   \u183 \'b7   Headings and names of quoted authorities in the text in red (for the latter there are sometimes instructions in the margins, e.g. \ldblquote Au\rdblquote  for Augustine, \ldblquote B\rdblquote  for Bernard of Clairvaux, \ldblquote O\rdblquote  for Origen). Red stroking of the majuscules. Plain initials in red on ff. 28r, 31r (both 2 lines), 54r (3 lines, after the heading >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Hie hebt sich an die marter des gecre\u252 \'fctzigten\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 <); 1, 2 or 3 lines on ff. 141r, 142r, 147r, 152v, 158r, 161r, 162r, 163r and v, 165r and v, 167v. Decorated initial (6 lines) in purple on gold background with floral engraving, in a rectangular trompe-l\rquote oeil frame in the shape of a green and red stone slab, on f. 2r; with vegetal border (acanthuses in purple, blue, green and yellow in the four margins). On the facing page (f. 1v) full-page miniature in a similar frame and with a similar engraved background in gold: the Annunciation, with God the Father in the upper left corner. Border decoration: at the four corners and in the middle of the sides a golden ball with sprays in ink; [K. S.: scattered notes for rubricator in the lower margin, mostly cut off].}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 The two sections of the manuscript, by two different scribes, are closely linked and strictly contemporary. In how far the miniature, with its rather inappropriate iconography, is original has to be investigated; it anyhow has the same decoration as the facing page f. 2r. On the pastedowns, scribbles in s. XVI Cursiva, mostly difficult to decipher: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Das biechlin ist des Hanns von dem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (\u8230 \'85) (front pastedown); \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 Das buchlin ist Jacobs Wid\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 (\u8230 \'85) (end pastedown). Collection of Adalbert Freiherr von Lanna-Prag (1836\endash 1909); his bookplate on the front pastedown, with the handwritten shelf-mark \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 IX.B.44\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 . Sale of the Lanna-Prag collection by Gilhofer and Ranschburg, Vienna 1911 (catalogue, no. 9, with the wrong title \ldblquote Das Buch der Sch\u246 \'f6pfungen\rdblquote ). [K. S.: Sold by Antiquariat J. Halle, Munich 1912 (catalogue, no. 277). E. L. McAdam, jr. and George Milne (New York) purchased it in 1955 from the antiquarian bookshop Horace G. Commin., Bournemouth (antiquarian: Alan Gradon Thomas [1911\endash 1992], see note on f. Iv: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 South German signed a. dated 1475, \u163 \'a3 21.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ). Other shelf marks or acquisition numbers in pencil: on front flyleaf recto \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 195760\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , on the front pastedown: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 a 23471.\\ AU9.-\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (?).] Purchased on the Edwin J. Beinecke Fund [K. S.: see bookplate on the end flyleaf] from Antiquariat J\u246 \'f6rn G\u252 \'fcnther, Hamburg, in 1992.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 [K. S.: Dialect: Upper German (with characteristics of Swabian and northern Upper German [Nurembergian]).]}

