\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \endash  3\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Computus Iudaicus, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Prolog, 1.1\endash 5.2, vier Tabellen. Prolog: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Me pudet Iudeum audire talia scire / Deberet clericus noscereque pocius / Me piget et miseret simul et tedet quod appellat / Iudeus clerum per sibi nota preit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hanc concordetur nobiscum et referetur.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text: : \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Qui virtutes vocabulorum sunt ignari de facili paraloyzantur ut dicit Aristoteles primo elencorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ante mediam noctem et sex post et sic patet concordia in cuncti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 s\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  et sic finitus est conputus Iudaicus.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit hoc totum infunde \u8224 \'86.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \endash  Fr\u252 \'fche vollst\u228 \'e4ndige Version des Computus Iudaicus. Ed.: C. Philipp E. Nothaft, Medieval Latin Christian Texts on the Jewish Calendar. A Study with Five Editions and Translations (Time, Astronomy, and Calendars 4), Leiden \endash  Boston 2014, S. 442\endash 466 (mit Abweichungen und Erg\u228 \'e4nzungen). Zu Werk und \u220 \'dcberlieferung vgl. ebd., S. 378\endash 441 (ohne diese Hs.). Vgl. Lynn Thorndike / Pearl Kibre, A Catalogue of Incipits of Mediaeval Scientific Writings in Latin, Cambridge/Mass. 1963, Sp. 854; Walther, Initia Nr. 10842.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 3\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash  10\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Johannes de Sacrobosco]: Algorismus vulgaris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Omnia, que aprimeva\~\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  rerum origine processerunt, ratione numerorum formata sunt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \u8230 \'85 \endash  \u8230 \'85 \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et hoc \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  de radicum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 extractione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26  dicta sufficiant, tam in numeris quadratis quam in cubitis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Explicit algorismus etc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \endash  Ed.: Petri Philomeni de Dacia in Algorismum vulgarem Johannis de Sacrobosco commentarius, hg. v. Maximilian Curtze, Kopenhagen 1897, S. 1\endash 19 (mit Abweichungen und leichten K\u252 \'fcrzungen); Petri Philomenae de Dacia et Petri de S. Audomaro. Teil 1: Opera Petri Philomenae, hg. v. Fritz Saaby Pedersen (Corpus philosophorum Danicorum medii aevi 10,1), Kopenhagen 1983, S. 174\endash 201. Vgl. Thorndike, 1937, Sp. 463; Thorndike/Kibre 991; Hamesse/Szyller Nr. 22832.}

